{"jobs":[{"id":"0e6e395c-5692-4b33-9005-151ae576e636","title":"Fullstack Engineer","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-03-30T21:51:41.665+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Los Angeles"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/atticus/0e6e395c-5692-4b33-9005-151ae576e636","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/atticus/0e6e395c-5692-4b33-9005-151ae576e636/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2><strong>About Atticus</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At any given time, 16 million Americans are experiencing a crisis that requires urgent help from our legal system or government. The right assistance could transform their lives. But today, most never get it.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Atticus makes it easy for any sick or injured American to get life-changing aid. Our mission is to tear down barriers between people in crisis and the aid they deserve. In the last six years, we’ve become the leading platform connecting people with disabilities to government benefits.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We also help victims of accidents, misconduct, and violence get compensation from insurance. So far, we’ve helped hundreds of thousands of people access over $10 billion in life-changing aid —and earned over 20,000 five-star reviews. And we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We've raised more than $100 million from top VC firms like Fika, Forerunner, Google Ventures, and True Ventures, and we’re on our way to creating a category defining business assisting needy Americans.</p><h2><strong>The Job</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Atticus works in an industry dominated by outdated technology that is ripe for fresh thinking: our core competitors rely on massive call centers to screen clients, antiquated CRMs to track and manage cases, and paper checks to get paid (provided they’re sent to the right address).</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Conversely, as a VC-backed tech company our product &amp; engineering department powers everything we do: from creating an engaging online experience for people in crisis to providing tools for our network lawyers as they serve our clients, Atticus relies on technology to fulfill our mission.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We’re looking for backend-focused fullstack Software Engineers to join our Representation pod, a team of engineers, product managers, and designers building the core tools that help law firms deliver consistent, quality experiences for their clients. The team works closely with our in-house law firm, rapidly iterating to understand real workflows and turn complex legal processes into intuitive, scalable software.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You’ll work across the stack with a backend focus, and will partner with every department at Atticus as we continue to grow our platform to help people in need find trusted legal support.</p><h2><strong> What You'll Do:</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design, build and operate Atticus’ web applications with a focus on performance, modularity, extensibility, and reliability</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work with product and design to evaluate and refine product details and acceptance criteria</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Architect, design, write, review, and test code in a collaborative environment with other software engineers</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Leverage your peers as multipliers for your skills to create excellent products and services</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The role is a rare opportunity to join a fast-growing Series C startup that doubles as a B-corp social enterprise. Every project you take on will help clients in need get the help they deserve, and you’ll shape our company culture as we scale. We’re looking for engineers who are excited about our mission and the challenges it entails.</p><h2><strong>Qualifications</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Required:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You have 3+ years of experience building production full-stack applications using modern languages and frameworks</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You have experience building and optimizing React-based user interfaces</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You have experience designing and operating reliable, scalable backend systems and APIs</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You partner closely with product and design to clarify requirements and deliver user-focused solutions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You demonstrate good judgment around code quality, including when and how to test</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You are comfortable owning services in production, including deployment, monitoring, and troubleshooting</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bonus / Nice-to-Have:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with Google Cloud Platform, Kubernetes, Terraform, Docker, Golang</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You have experience building software for industries with complex workflows and long-standing practices, such as legal, healthcare, or financial services</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You have experience evolving systems as teams and traffic scale</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You’re interested in improving internal tooling, developer experience, or team processes</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are strongly committed to building a diverse team. If you’re from a background that’s underrepresented in tech, we’d love to meet you.</p><h2><strong>Salary and Benefits</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare opportunity to join a startup that has strong traction (substantial funding, well-respected backers, tremendous growth, and many happy customers) but is still small enough that you can have a huge impact and play a role in shaping our culture.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We’re a certified B Corporation tackling a critical social problem. Our mission to help people in need drives everything we do, and your work here will touch many lives.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We offer competitive pay — including equity for all employees — and generous benefits:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Medical and dental insurance with 100% of premiums covered for employees and their families</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">15 vacation days &amp; ~20 paid holidays each year (including two weeks at end-of-year)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Free membership to OneMedical</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$600/year internet stipend</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$1,000/year reimbursable stipend for education and training outside of work</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Up to $1,200/year student loan repayment assistance</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">401(k) and optional HSA/FSA</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Humble, thoughtful, smart, fun colleagues</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We anticipate the base salary band for this role will be between $157,250 and $230,000 in addition to equity and benefits. The salary at offer will be determined by a number of factors such as candidate’s experience, knowledge, skills and abilities, as well as internal equity among our team.</p><h2><strong>Location</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This job is fully remote and we’re committed to empowering everyone with flexibility. Work remotely, and travel to LA (on the company dime) as needed to be with your colleagues – usually quarterly, plus offsites. We care a lot about building a great culture and we think some interactions need to happen in person, so we put a lot of thought into retreats, offsites, and other ways to gather.</p>","descriptionPlain":"ABOUT ATTICUS\n\nAt any given time, 16 million Americans are experiencing a crisis that requires urgent help from our legal system or government. The right assistance could transform their lives. But today, most never get it.\n\nAtticus makes it easy for any sick or injured American to get life-changing aid. Our mission is to tear down barriers between people in crisis and the aid they deserve. In the last six years, we’ve become the leading platform connecting people with disabilities to government benefits.\n\nWe also help victims of accidents, misconduct, and violence get compensation from insurance. So far, we’ve helped hundreds of thousands of people access over $10 billion in life-changing aid —and earned over 20,000 five-star reviews. And we’re just getting started.\n\nWe've raised more than $100 million from top VC firms like Fika, Forerunner, Google Ventures, and True Ventures, and we’re on our way to creating a category defining business assisting needy Americans.\n\n\nTHE JOB\n\nAtticus works in an industry dominated by outdated technology that is ripe for fresh thinking: our core competitors rely on massive call centers to screen clients, antiquated CRMs to track and manage cases, and paper checks to get paid (provided they’re sent to the right address).\n\nConversely, as a VC-backed tech company our product & engineering department powers everything we do: from creating an engaging online experience for people in crisis to providing tools for our network lawyers as they serve our clients, Atticus relies on technology to fulfill our mission.\n\nWe’re looking for backend-focused fullstack Software Engineers to join our Representation pod, a team of engineers, product managers, and designers building the core tools that help law firms deliver consistent, quality experiences for their clients. The team works closely with our in-house law firm, rapidly iterating to understand real workflows and turn complex legal processes into intuitive, scalable software.\n\nYou’ll work across the stack with a backend focus, and will partner with every department at Atticus as we continue to grow our platform to help people in need find trusted legal support.\n\n\n WHAT YOU'LL DO:\n\n - Design, build and operate Atticus’ web applications with a focus on performance, modularity, extensibility, and reliability\n\n - Work with product and design to evaluate and refine product details and acceptance criteria\n\n - Architect, design, write, review, and test code in a collaborative environment with other software engineers\n\n - Leverage your peers as multipliers for your skills to create excellent products and services\n\nThe role is a rare opportunity to join a fast-growing Series C startup that doubles as a B-corp social enterprise. Every project you take on will help clients in need get the help they deserve, and you’ll shape our company culture as we scale. We’re looking for engineers who are excited about our mission and the challenges it entails.\n\n\nQUALIFICATIONS\n\nRequired:\n\n - You have 3+ years of experience building production full-stack applications using modern languages and frameworks\n\n - You have experience building and optimizing React-based user interfaces\n\n - You have experience designing and operating reliable, scalable backend systems and APIs\n\n - You partner closely with product and design to clarify requirements and deliver user-focused solutions\n\n - You demonstrate good judgment around code quality, including when and how to test\n\n - You are comfortable owning services in production, including deployment, monitoring, and troubleshooting\n\nBonus / Nice-to-Have:\n\n - Experience with Google Cloud Platform, Kubernetes, Terraform, Docker, Golang\n\n - You have experience building software for industries with complex workflows and long-standing practices, such as legal, healthcare, or financial services\n\n - You have experience evolving systems as teams and traffic scale\n\n - You’re interested in improving internal tooling, developer experience, or team processes\n\nWe are strongly committed to building a diverse team. If you’re from a background that’s underrepresented in tech, we’d love to meet you.\n\n\nSALARY AND BENEFITS\n\nThis is a rare opportunity to join a startup that has strong traction (substantial funding, well-respected backers, tremendous growth, and many happy customers) but is still small enough that you can have a huge impact and play a role in shaping our culture.\n\nWe’re a certified B Corporation tackling a critical social problem. Our mission to help people in need drives everything we do, and your work here will touch many lives.\n\nWe offer competitive pay — including equity for all employees — and generous benefits:\n\n - Medical and dental insurance with 100% of premiums covered for employees and their families\n\n - 15 vacation days & ~20 paid holidays each year (including two weeks at end-of-year)\n\n - Free membership to OneMedical\n\n - $600/year internet stipend\n\n - $1,000/year reimbursable stipend for education and training outside of work\n\n - Up to $1,200/year student loan repayment assistance\n\n - 401(k) and optional HSA/FSA\n\n - Humble, thoughtful, smart, fun colleagues\n\nWe anticipate the base salary band for this role will be between $157,250 and $230,000 in addition to equity and benefits. The salary at offer will be determined by a number of factors such as candidate’s experience, knowledge, skills and abilities, as well as internal equity among our team.\n\n\nLOCATION\n\nThis job is fully remote and we’re committed to empowering everyone with flexibility. Work remotely, and travel to LA (on the company dime) as needed to be with your colleagues – usually quarterly, plus offsites. We care a lot about building a great culture and we think some interactions need to happen in person, so we put a lot of thought into retreats, offsites, and other ways to gather.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"37661fa1-aef8-4cb3-854d-7bc5e8e7fc3d","title":"Business Operations Lead","department":"Operations","team":"Operations","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2025-02-07T22:49:10.446+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Los Angeles"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/atticus/37661fa1-aef8-4cb3-854d-7bc5e8e7fc3d","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/atticus/37661fa1-aef8-4cb3-854d-7bc5e8e7fc3d/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2><strong>About Atticus</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At any given time, 16 million Americans are experiencing a crisis that requires urgent help from our legal system or government. The right assistance could transform their lives. But today, most never get it.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Atticus makes it easy for any sick or injured American to get life-changing aid. Our mission is to tear down barriers between people in crisis and the aid they deserve. In the last six years, we’ve become the leading platform connecting people with disabilities to government benefits.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We also help victims of accidents, misconduct, and violence get compensation from insurance. So far, we’ve helped hundreds of thousands of people access over $10 billion in life-changing aid —and earned over 20,000 five-star reviews. And we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We’ve raised more than $100 million from top VC firms like Fika, Forerunner, Google Ventures, and True Ventures, and we’re on our way to creating a category defining business assisting Americans in need.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Where we are today:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Last year we raised a $50M Series C, valuing Atticus at $450M.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our primary vertical (Disability) is profitable and will reach a ~$90M revenue run-rate by the end of this year</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We’ve kicked off our Injury vertical with a small but scrappy team working on the offering and GTM approach.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>The Job</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our business is complex and multi-faceted: We play in an enormous space with huge barriers to entry, we have no direct competitors, and as a two-sided marketplace we have to coordinate multiple constituencies via a complex funnel with some parts that are all tech and others that are fully human. Every day we face new operating challenges that require someone to quickly gather data, make a decision, and execute.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">So, in addition to software engineers, lawyers, and marketers, our team includes a bunch of ex-consultants (our CEO is a BCG alum and we’ve built a small BizOps org from BCG, Bain and McKinsey). To a level that’s unusual among our peer startups, we’re investing in building a top-tier Strategy &amp; Business Operations team that oversees the core of our business and drives key projects, and we’re hiring several more consultants to join it.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This job mixes things in any good consultant’s comfort zone (devising strategy, managing and coordinating projects, gathering and analyzing data) with responsibilities unique to being an operator in a fast-growing tech company (user research, product development, growth marketing, venture finance). Typical projects you’d own:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design, test, and ship a site experiment for our new Injury vertical to qualify and convert clients.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Find the gaps in our client service operations and lead the project that cuts our costs to serve each client by 25%.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Rebuild the model that predicts what each case is worth, and wire it into how we bid on ads and forecast the business.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Stand up and run a new QA function: build the tooling and interface, design the process, and train the team.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Qualifications</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Required:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You were/are at a top consulting firm and thrived there.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You’ve led ambiguous projects end-to-end: framed the question, owned a complex model, made the call, and worked hand-in-hand with the client team to implement.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You’re excited to own our toughest modeling workstreams.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You’re a kind and thoughtful colleague who knows how to shape a great team culture, persuasively advocate for your ideas, and get buy-in from others.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You have a demonstrated commitment to doing good and helping people.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bonus / Nice-to-Have:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You took on management ahead of tenure (e.g., EM at McKinsey, mini-PL at BCG, Manager at Bain).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You have experience with marketplace businesses or complex consumer services (insurance, fintech, medical, real estate, etc.).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You’ve done consumer-focused research or discovery work, or something else that makes you comfortable interviewing and empathizing with people from all walks of life.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are strongly committed to building a diverse team. If you’re from a background that’s underrepresented in tech, we’d love to meet you</p><h2><strong>Salary and Benefits</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare opportunity to join a startup that has strong traction (substantial funding, well-respected backers, tremendous growth, and many happy customers) but is still small enough that you can have a huge impact and play a role in shaping our culture.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We’re a certified B Corporation tackling a critical social problem. Our mission to help people in need drives everything we do, and your work here will touch many lives.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We offer competitive pay — including equity for all employees — and generous benefits:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Medical and dental insurance with 100% of premiums covered for employees and their families</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">15 vacation days &amp; ~20 paid holidays each year (including two weeks at end-of-year)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Free membership to OneMedical</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$600/year internet stipend</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$1,000/year reimbursable stipend for education and training outside of work</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Up to $1,200/year student loan repayment assistance</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">401(k) and optional HSA/FSA</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Humble, thoughtful, smart, fun colleagues</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We anticipate the base salary band for this role will be between $150,000 to $190,000 in addition to equity and benefits. The salary at offer will be determined by a number of factors such as candidate’s experience, knowledge, skills and abilities, as well as internal equity among our team.</p><h2><strong>Location</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This job is fully remote and we’re committed to empowering everyone with flexibility. Work remotely, and travel to LA (on the company dime) as needed to be with your colleagues – usually quarterly, plus offsites. We care a lot about building a great culture and we think some interactions need to happen in person, so we put a lot of thought into retreats, offsites, and other ways to gather.</p>","descriptionPlain":"ABOUT ATTICUS\n\nAt any given time, 16 million Americans are experiencing a crisis that requires urgent help from our legal system or government. The right assistance could transform their lives. But today, most never get it.\n\nAtticus makes it easy for any sick or injured American to get life-changing aid. Our mission is to tear down barriers between people in crisis and the aid they deserve. In the last six years, we’ve become the leading platform connecting people with disabilities to government benefits.\n\nWe also help victims of accidents, misconduct, and violence get compensation from insurance. So far, we’ve helped hundreds of thousands of people access over $10 billion in life-changing aid —and earned over 20,000 five-star reviews. And we’re just getting started.\n\nWe’ve raised more than $100 million from top VC firms like Fika, Forerunner, Google Ventures, and True Ventures, and we’re on our way to creating a category defining business assisting Americans in need.\n\nWhere we are today:\n\n - Last year we raised a $50M Series C, valuing Atticus at $450M.\n\n - Our primary vertical (Disability) is profitable and will reach a ~$90M revenue run-rate by the end of this year\n\n - We’ve kicked off our Injury vertical with a small but scrappy team working on the offering and GTM approach.\n\n\nTHE JOB\n\nOur business is complex and multi-faceted: We play in an enormous space with huge barriers to entry, we have no direct competitors, and as a two-sided marketplace we have to coordinate multiple constituencies via a complex funnel with some parts that are all tech and others that are fully human. Every day we face new operating challenges that require someone to quickly gather data, make a decision, and execute.\n\nSo, in addition to software engineers, lawyers, and marketers, our team includes a bunch of ex-consultants (our CEO is a BCG alum and we’ve built a small BizOps org from BCG, Bain and McKinsey). To a level that’s unusual among our peer startups, we’re investing in building a top-tier Strategy & Business Operations team that oversees the core of our business and drives key projects, and we’re hiring several more consultants to join it.\n\nThis job mixes things in any good consultant’s comfort zone (devising strategy, managing and coordinating projects, gathering and analyzing data) with responsibilities unique to being an operator in a fast-growing tech company (user research, product development, growth marketing, venture finance). Typical projects you’d own:\n\n - Design, test, and ship a site experiment for our new Injury vertical to qualify and convert clients.\n\n - Find the gaps in our client service operations and lead the project that cuts our costs to serve each client by 25%.\n\n - Rebuild the model that predicts what each case is worth, and wire it into how we bid on ads and forecast the business.\n\n - Stand up and run a new QA function: build the tooling and interface, design the process, and train the team.\n\n\nQUALIFICATIONS\n\nRequired:\n\n - You were/are at a top consulting firm and thrived there.\n\n - You’ve led ambiguous projects end-to-end: framed the question, owned a complex model, made the call, and worked hand-in-hand with the client team to implement.\n\n - You’re excited to own our toughest modeling workstreams.\n\n - You’re a kind and thoughtful colleague who knows how to shape a great team culture, persuasively advocate for your ideas, and get buy-in from others.\n\n - You have a demonstrated commitment to doing good and helping people.\n\nBonus / Nice-to-Have:\n\n - You took on management ahead of tenure (e.g., EM at McKinsey, mini-PL at BCG, Manager at Bain).\n\n - You have experience with marketplace businesses or complex consumer services (insurance, fintech, medical, real estate, etc.).\n\n - You’ve done consumer-focused research or discovery work, or something else that makes you comfortable interviewing and empathizing with people from all walks of life.\n\nWe are strongly committed to building a diverse team. If you’re from a background that’s underrepresented in tech, we’d love to meet you\n\n\nSALARY AND BENEFITS\n\nThis is a rare opportunity to join a startup that has strong traction (substantial funding, well-respected backers, tremendous growth, and many happy customers) but is still small enough that you can have a huge impact and play a role in shaping our culture.\n\nWe’re a certified B Corporation tackling a critical social problem. Our mission to help people in need drives everything we do, and your work here will touch many lives.\n\nWe offer competitive pay — including equity for all employees — and generous benefits:\n\n - Medical and dental insurance with 100% of premiums covered for employees and their families\n\n - 15 vacation days & ~20 paid holidays each year (including two weeks at end-of-year)\n\n - Free membership to OneMedical\n\n - $600/year internet stipend\n\n - $1,000/year reimbursable stipend for education and training outside of work\n\n - Up to $1,200/year student loan repayment assistance\n\n - 401(k) and optional HSA/FSA\n\n - Humble, thoughtful, smart, fun colleagues\n\nWe anticipate the base salary band for this role will be between $150,000 to $190,000 in addition to equity and benefits. The salary at offer will be determined by a number of factors such as candidate’s experience, knowledge, skills and abilities, as well as internal equity among our team.\n\n\nLOCATION\n\nThis job is fully remote and we’re committed to empowering everyone with flexibility. Work remotely, and travel to LA (on the company dime) as needed to be with your colleagues – usually quarterly, plus offsites. We care a lot about building a great culture and we think some interactions need to happen in person, so we put a lot of thought into retreats, offsites, and other ways to gather.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"d2996efc-c8b0-4b9c-a840-c8750fc6d127","title":"Client Experience Associate","department":"Client Experience","team":"Client Experience","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-06-18T16:47:56.777+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Los Angeles"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/atticus/d2996efc-c8b0-4b9c-a840-c8750fc6d127","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/atticus/d2996efc-c8b0-4b9c-a840-c8750fc6d127/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2><strong>About Atticus</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At any given time, 16 million Americans are experiencing a crisis that requires urgent help from our legal system or government. The right assistance could transform their lives. But today, most never get it.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Atticus makes it easy for any sick or injured American to get life-changing aid. Our mission is to tear down barriers between people in crisis and the aid they deserve. In the last six years, we’ve become the leading platform connecting people with disabilities to government benefits.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We also help victims of accidents, misconduct, and violence get compensation from insurance. So far, we’ve helped hundreds of thousands of people access over $10 billion in life-changing aid —and earned over 20,000 five-star reviews. And we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We've raised more than $100 million from top VC firms like Fika, Forerunner, Google Ventures, and True Ventures, and we’re on our way to creating a category defining business assisting needy Americans.</p><h2><strong>The Job</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Each day, hundreds of people seek our help getting disability benefits or insurance compensation. They’re intimidated by the process, unsure where to turn, and desperate for good advice.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As part of our Client Experience team, your job is to get them on the right path. You’ll spend each day communicating on the phone with clients to understand their situation, figure out whether we can help them, and advise them on the next steps. You'll become an expert on a complex and interesting field, learn to rapidly navigate our internal tech platforms and tools (Salesforce, etc.), and help hundreds of ordinary people (each with a unique story) every week. You’ll be measured by and compensated for the impact you have on our clients. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This job is different from traditional customer service or sales: Our service is totally free, and clients are desperate for our help — so you'll rarely talk to an angry customer. The conversations are deeply rewarding, and clients are profoundly grateful. You will have to navigate conversations on deeply personal and sad topics, gently but quickly offer guidance, and handle many different interactions over the course of a day. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Please note: You don’t need any prior legal knowledge or experience to excel in this job.</p><h2><strong>Qualifications</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Required:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You have a Bachelor’s degree from a four-year university with strong academic performance.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You have at least 1 year of working experience outside of internships (longer internships to be considered).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You care about people and can interact with folks from all walks of life; you’re able to simultaneously be supportive to a person in crisis and quickly drive a conversation.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You’re a quick learner and a competent writer, able to master complex new topics and platforms when given instruction and support.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You have a strong work ethic and are capable of juggling multiple competing priorities.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bonus / Nice-to-Have:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You’ve previously worked at a high volume, high-performing service/sales/support team from a company known for great customer service.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You have completed a socially-focused, hands-on internship or have significant volunteer experience.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are strongly committed to building a diverse team. If you’re from a background that’s underrepresented in tech, we’d love to meet you.</p><h2><strong>Salary and Benefits</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare opportunity to join a startup that has strong traction (substantial funding, well-respected backers, tremendous growth, and many happy customers) but is still small enough that you can have a huge impact and play a role in shaping our culture.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We’re a certified B Corporation tackling a critical social problem. Our mission to help people in need drives everything we do, and your work here will touch many lives.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We offer competitive pay — including equity for all employees — and generous benefits:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Medical and dental insurance with 100% of premiums covered for employees and their families</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">15 vacation days &amp; ~20 paid holidays each year (including two weeks at the end-of-year)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Free membership to OneMedical</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$600/year stipend for internet service</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$1,000/year reimbursable stipend for education and training outside of work</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Up to $1,200/year student loan repayment assistance</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">401(k) and optional HSA/FSA</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Humble, thoughtful, smart, fun colleagues </p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We anticipate the base salary band for this role will be between $50,000 and $60,000 in addition to equity, benefits, and an uncapped monthly bonus structure. Under the current bonus compensation plan, top performers are earning over $75,000 in total cash compensation. The salary at offer will be determined by a number of factors such as candidate’s experience, knowledge, skills, and abilities, as well as internal equity among our team.</p><h2><strong>Location</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This job is fully remote and we’re committed to empowering everyone with flexibility. We care a lot about building a great culture and we think some interactions need to happen in person, so we put a lot of thought into retreats, offsites, and other ways to gather.</p>","descriptionPlain":"ABOUT ATTICUS\n\nAt any given time, 16 million Americans are experiencing a crisis that requires urgent help from our legal system or government. The right assistance could transform their lives. But today, most never get it.\n\nAtticus makes it easy for any sick or injured American to get life-changing aid. Our mission is to tear down barriers between people in crisis and the aid they deserve. In the last six years, we’ve become the leading platform connecting people with disabilities to government benefits.\n\nWe also help victims of accidents, misconduct, and violence get compensation from insurance. So far, we’ve helped hundreds of thousands of people access over $10 billion in life-changing aid —and earned over 20,000 five-star reviews. And we’re just getting started.\n\nWe've raised more than $100 million from top VC firms like Fika, Forerunner, Google Ventures, and True Ventures, and we’re on our way to creating a category defining business assisting needy Americans.\n\n\nTHE JOB\n\nEach day, hundreds of people seek our help getting disability benefits or insurance compensation. They’re intimidated by the process, unsure where to turn, and desperate for good advice.\n\nAs part of our Client Experience team, your job is to get them on the right path. You’ll spend each day communicating on the phone with clients to understand their situation, figure out whether we can help them, and advise them on the next steps. You'll become an expert on a complex and interesting field, learn to rapidly navigate our internal tech platforms and tools (Salesforce, etc.), and help hundreds of ordinary people (each with a unique story) every week. You’ll be measured by and compensated for the impact you have on our clients. \n\nThis job is different from traditional customer service or sales: Our service is totally free, and clients are desperate for our help — so you'll rarely talk to an angry customer. The conversations are deeply rewarding, and clients are profoundly grateful. You will have to navigate conversations on deeply personal and sad topics, gently but quickly offer guidance, and handle many different interactions over the course of a day. \n\nPlease note: You don’t need any prior legal knowledge or experience to excel in this job.\n\n\nQUALIFICATIONS\n\nRequired:\n\n - You have a Bachelor’s degree from a four-year university with strong academic performance.\n\n - You have at least 1 year of working experience outside of internships (longer internships to be considered).\n\n - You care about people and can interact with folks from all walks of life; you’re able to simultaneously be supportive to a person in crisis and quickly drive a conversation.\n\n - You’re a quick learner and a competent writer, able to master complex new topics and platforms when given instruction and support.\n\n - You have a strong work ethic and are capable of juggling multiple competing priorities.\n\nBonus / Nice-to-Have:\n\n - You’ve previously worked at a high volume, high-performing service/sales/support team from a company known for great customer service.\n\n - You have completed a socially-focused, hands-on internship or have significant volunteer experience.\n\nWe are strongly committed to building a diverse team. If you’re from a background that’s underrepresented in tech, we’d love to meet you.\n\n\nSALARY AND BENEFITS\n\nThis is a rare opportunity to join a startup that has strong traction (substantial funding, well-respected backers, tremendous growth, and many happy customers) but is still small enough that you can have a huge impact and play a role in shaping our culture.\n\nWe’re a certified B Corporation tackling a critical social problem. Our mission to help people in need drives everything we do, and your work here will touch many lives.\n\nWe offer competitive pay — including equity for all employees — and generous benefits:\n\n - Medical and dental insurance with 100% of premiums covered for employees and their families\n\n - 15 vacation days & ~20 paid holidays each year (including two weeks at the end-of-year)\n\n - Free membership to OneMedical\n\n - $600/year stipend for internet service\n\n - $1,000/year reimbursable stipend for education and training outside of work\n\n - Up to $1,200/year student loan repayment assistance\n\n - 401(k) and optional HSA/FSA\n\n - Humble, thoughtful, smart, fun colleagues \n\nWe anticipate the base salary band for this role will be between $50,000 and $60,000 in addition to equity, benefits, and an uncapped monthly bonus structure. Under the current bonus compensation plan, top performers are earning over $75,000 in total cash compensation. The salary at offer will be determined by a number of factors such as candidate’s experience, knowledge, skills, and abilities, as well as internal equity among our team.\n\n\nLOCATION\n\nThis job is fully remote and we’re committed to empowering everyone with flexibility. We care a lot about building a great culture and we think some interactions need to happen in person, so we put a lot of thought into retreats, offsites, and other ways to gather.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"c9c2a0a8-4049-4c19-932f-b3a4979a0479","title":"Client Experience Specialist","department":"Client Experience","team":"Client Experience","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-06-18T16:49:21.974+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Los Angeles"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/atticus/c9c2a0a8-4049-4c19-932f-b3a4979a0479","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/atticus/c9c2a0a8-4049-4c19-932f-b3a4979a0479/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2><strong>About Atticus</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At any given time, 16 million Americans are experiencing a crisis that requires urgent help from our legal system or government. The right assistance could transform their lives. But today, most never get it.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Atticus makes it easy for any sick or injured American to get life-changing aid. Our mission is to tear down barriers between people in crisis and the aid they deserve. In the last six years, we’ve become the leading platform connecting people with disabilities to government benefits.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We also help victims of accidents, misconduct, and violence get compensation from insurance. So far, we’ve helped hundreds of thousands of people access over $10 billion in life-changing aid —and earned over 20,000 five-star reviews. And we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We've raised more than $100 million from top VC firms like Fika, Forerunner, Google Ventures, and True Ventures, and we’re on our way to creating a category defining business assisting needy Americans.</p><h2><strong>The Job</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Each day, hundreds of people seek our help getting disability benefits or insurance compensation. They’re intimidated by the process, unsure where to turn, and desperate for good advice.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As part of our Client Experience team, your job is to get them on the right path. You’ll spend each day communicating on the phone with clients to understand their situation, figure out whether we can help them, and advise them on the next steps. You'll become an expert on a complex and interesting field, learn to rapidly navigate our internal tech platforms and tools (Salesforce, etc.), and help hundreds of ordinary people (each with a unique story) every week. You’ll be measured by and compensated for the impact you have on our clients. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This job is different from traditional customer service or sales: Our service is totally free, and clients are desperate for our help — so you'll rarely talk to an angry customer. The conversations are deeply rewarding, and clients are profoundly grateful. You will have to navigate conversations on deeply personal and sad topics, gently but quickly offer guidance, and handle many different interactions over the course of a day. </p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Please note: You don’t need any prior legal knowledge or experience to excel in this job.</p><h2><strong>Qualifications</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Required:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You have at least three years of professional work experience, and have succeeded in jobs that involve talking to customers all day (CX, sales, support, hospitality, etc.).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You care about people and can interact with folks from all walks of life; you’re able to simultaneously be supportive to a person in crisis and quickly drive a conversation.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You’re a quick learner and a competent writer, able to master complex new topics and platforms when given instruction and support.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Preferred:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You’ve had a metrics-driven role and you exceeded the goals set for you and outperformed your peers.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You've previously worked at high volume, high-performing service/sales/support team from a company known for great customer service.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are strongly committed to building a diverse team. If you’re from a background that’s underrepresented in tech, we’d love to meet you.</p><h2><strong>Salary and Benefits</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare opportunity to join a startup that has strong traction (substantial funding, well-respected backers, tremendous growth, and many happy customers) but is still small enough that you can have a huge impact and play a role in shaping our culture.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We’re a certified B Corporation tackling a critical social problem. Our mission to help people in need drives everything we do, and your work here will touch many lives.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We offer competitive pay — including equity for all employees, bonus, and generous benefits:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Medical and dental insurance with 100% of premiums covered for employees and their families</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">15 vacation days &amp; ~20 paid holidays each year (including two weeks at end-of-year)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Free membership to OneMedical</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$600/year stipend for internet service</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$1,000/year reimbursable stipend for education and training outside of work</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Up to $1,200/year student loan repayment assistance</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">401(k) and optional HSA/FSA</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Humble, thoughtful, smart, fun colleagues </p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We anticipate the base salary band for this role will be between $60,000 and $75,000 in addition to equity, benefits, and an uncapped monthly bonus structure. Under the current bonus compensation plan, top performers are earning over $100,000 in total cash compensation. The salary at offer will be determined by a number of factors such as candidate’s experience, knowledge, skills, and abilities, as well as internal equity among our team.</p><h2><strong>Location</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This job is fully remote and we’re committed to empowering everyone with flexibility. We care a lot about building a great culture and we think some interactions need to happen in person, so we put a lot of thought into retreats, offsites, and other ways to gather.</p>","descriptionPlain":"ABOUT ATTICUS\n\nAt any given time, 16 million Americans are experiencing a crisis that requires urgent help from our legal system or government. The right assistance could transform their lives. But today, most never get it.\n\nAtticus makes it easy for any sick or injured American to get life-changing aid. Our mission is to tear down barriers between people in crisis and the aid they deserve. In the last six years, we’ve become the leading platform connecting people with disabilities to government benefits.\n\nWe also help victims of accidents, misconduct, and violence get compensation from insurance. So far, we’ve helped hundreds of thousands of people access over $10 billion in life-changing aid —and earned over 20,000 five-star reviews. And we’re just getting started.\n\nWe've raised more than $100 million from top VC firms like Fika, Forerunner, Google Ventures, and True Ventures, and we’re on our way to creating a category defining business assisting needy Americans.\n\n\nTHE JOB\n\nEach day, hundreds of people seek our help getting disability benefits or insurance compensation. They’re intimidated by the process, unsure where to turn, and desperate for good advice.\n\nAs part of our Client Experience team, your job is to get them on the right path. You’ll spend each day communicating on the phone with clients to understand their situation, figure out whether we can help them, and advise them on the next steps. You'll become an expert on a complex and interesting field, learn to rapidly navigate our internal tech platforms and tools (Salesforce, etc.), and help hundreds of ordinary people (each with a unique story) every week. You’ll be measured by and compensated for the impact you have on our clients. \n\nThis job is different from traditional customer service or sales: Our service is totally free, and clients are desperate for our help — so you'll rarely talk to an angry customer. The conversations are deeply rewarding, and clients are profoundly grateful. You will have to navigate conversations on deeply personal and sad topics, gently but quickly offer guidance, and handle many different interactions over the course of a day. \n\nPlease note: You don’t need any prior legal knowledge or experience to excel in this job.\n\n\nQUALIFICATIONS\n\nRequired:\n\n - You have at least three years of professional work experience, and have succeeded in jobs that involve talking to customers all day (CX, sales, support, hospitality, etc.).\n\n - You care about people and can interact with folks from all walks of life; you’re able to simultaneously be supportive to a person in crisis and quickly drive a conversation.\n\n - You’re a quick learner and a competent writer, able to master complex new topics and platforms when given instruction and support.\n\nPreferred:\n\n - You’ve had a metrics-driven role and you exceeded the goals set for you and outperformed your peers.\n\n - You've previously worked at high volume, high-performing service/sales/support team from a company known for great customer service.\n\nWe are strongly committed to building a diverse team. If you’re from a background that’s underrepresented in tech, we’d love to meet you.\n\n\nSALARY AND BENEFITS\n\nThis is a rare opportunity to join a startup that has strong traction (substantial funding, well-respected backers, tremendous growth, and many happy customers) but is still small enough that you can have a huge impact and play a role in shaping our culture.\n\nWe’re a certified B Corporation tackling a critical social problem. Our mission to help people in need drives everything we do, and your work here will touch many lives.\n\nWe offer competitive pay — including equity for all employees, bonus, and generous benefits:\n\n - Medical and dental insurance with 100% of premiums covered for employees and their families\n\n - 15 vacation days & ~20 paid holidays each year (including two weeks at end-of-year)\n\n - Free membership to OneMedical\n\n - $600/year stipend for internet service\n\n - $1,000/year reimbursable stipend for education and training outside of work\n\n - Up to $1,200/year student loan repayment assistance\n\n - 401(k) and optional HSA/FSA\n\n - Humble, thoughtful, smart, fun colleagues \n\nWe anticipate the base salary band for this role will be between $60,000 and $75,000 in addition to equity, benefits, and an uncapped monthly bonus structure. Under the current bonus compensation plan, top performers are earning over $100,000 in total cash compensation. The salary at offer will be determined by a number of factors such as candidate’s experience, knowledge, skills, and abilities, as well as internal equity among our team.\n\n\nLOCATION\n\nThis job is fully remote and we’re committed to empowering everyone with flexibility. We care a lot about building a great culture and we think some interactions need to happen in person, so we put a lot of thought into retreats, offsites, and other ways to gather.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"67f7fa65-55ab-4838-bc9d-f15a9c2ccfea","title":"Product Manager","department":"Product & Design","team":"Product & Design","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2025-03-06T18:14:00.263+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Los Angeles"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/atticus/67f7fa65-55ab-4838-bc9d-f15a9c2ccfea","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/atticus/67f7fa65-55ab-4838-bc9d-f15a9c2ccfea/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2><strong>About Atticus</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At any given time, 16 million Americans are experiencing a crisis that requires urgent help from our legal system or government. The right assistance could transform their lives. But today, most never get it.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Atticus makes it easy for any sick or injured American to get life-changing aid. Our mission is to tear down barriers between people in crisis and the aid they deserve. In the last six years, we’ve become the leading platform connecting people with disabilities to government benefits.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We also help victims of accidents, misconduct, and violence get compensation from insurance. So far, we’ve helped hundreds of thousands of people access over $10 billion in life-changing aid —and earned over 20,000 five-star reviews. And we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We've raised more than $100 million from top VC firms like Fika, Forerunner, Google Ventures, and True Ventures, and we’re on our way to creating a category defining business assisting needy Americans.</p><h2><strong>The Job</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At every step of our funnel, we aim to make choosing Atticus a no-brainer. Our platform covers a lot: evaluating a client’s case, giving advice, matching them with the right lawyer, formalizing the arrangement, and helping both parties work together as the case progresses. We hold ourselves to an incredibly high bar, because we know it results in life-changing aid for those in need.  A few examples of what we’re currently working on:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Improve an existing framework to match clients to the best law firm in our network available (for their case, geography, client and firm preferences, etc.) and work with the Data Science team to turn it into a reality.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Interview partner law firms to prioritize the next set of features we’ll build, then partner with Design and Engineering to craft a formal roadmap and mock up wireframes for our next product launch.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Leverage data from our call center and case details to optimize how and when we reach clients across mediums and throughout their case lifecycle.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build a core data platform to support multiple verticals at varying scales with model-driven decision making and personalization throughout the funnel.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Responsibilities</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Get to know our users - both clients and lawyers - and understand their needs.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Craft a product vision for our next phase of growth. Go deep on strategy: become an expert in our business model, current offering, and key milestones to inform your work.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Develop a comprehensive product roadmap and build alignment for it with stakeholders and senior leadership.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work with engineering and design to build and ship new products and features. Play the role of conductor, coordinating and empowering others.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own key targets and metrics. Collect and analyze data, and use it to drive decision-making at a company level. Propose hypotheses, run experiments, and iterate quickly.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Qualifications</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3+ years of product management experience, building and shipping products at scale</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Demonstrated success in setting a product vision and strategy, and the ability to speak thoughtfully about the key decisions and tradeoffs you made</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Knowledge of best practices (from past work in a high-performing organization) and the ability to instill a great product culture as we grow</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Great communication and people skills — shown by great reviews from PMs, engineers and designers you’ve worked with</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Mastery of data platforms and ability to do your own analysis</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A demonstrated commitment to doing good and helping people</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bonus: Early-stage startup experience - complex consumer business, two-sided marketplace, and/or B2B product</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Salary and Benefits</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare opportunity to join a startup that has strong traction (substantial funding, well-respected backers, tremendous growth, and many happy customers) but is still small enough that you can have a huge impact and play a role in shaping our culture.We’re a certified B Corporation tackling a critical social problem. Our mission to help people in need drives everything we do, and your work here will touch many lives.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We offer competitive pay — including equity for all employees — and generous benefits:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Medical and dental insurance with 100% of premiums covered for employees and their families</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">15 vacation days &amp; ~20 paid holidays each year (including two weeks at end-of-year)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Free membership to OneMedical</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$600/year internet stipend</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$1,000/year reimbursable stipend for education and training outside of work</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Up to $1,200/year student loan repayment assistance</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">401(k) and optional HSA/FSA</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Humble, thoughtful, smart, fun colleagues</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Location</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This job is fully remote and we’re committed to empowering everyone with flexibility. Work remotely, and travel to LA (on the company dime) as needed to be with your colleagues – usually quarterly, plus offsites. We care a lot about building a great culture and we think some interactions need to happen in person, so we put a lot of thought into retreats, offsites, and other ways to gather.</p>","descriptionPlain":"ABOUT ATTICUS\n\nAt any given time, 16 million Americans are experiencing a crisis that requires urgent help from our legal system or government. The right assistance could transform their lives. But today, most never get it.\n\nAtticus makes it easy for any sick or injured American to get life-changing aid. Our mission is to tear down barriers between people in crisis and the aid they deserve. In the last six years, we’ve become the leading platform connecting people with disabilities to government benefits.\n\nWe also help victims of accidents, misconduct, and violence get compensation from insurance. So far, we’ve helped hundreds of thousands of people access over $10 billion in life-changing aid —and earned over 20,000 five-star reviews. And we’re just getting started.\n\nWe've raised more than $100 million from top VC firms like Fika, Forerunner, Google Ventures, and True Ventures, and we’re on our way to creating a category defining business assisting needy Americans.\n\n\nTHE JOB\n\nAt every step of our funnel, we aim to make choosing Atticus a no-brainer. Our platform covers a lot: evaluating a client’s case, giving advice, matching them with the right lawyer, formalizing the arrangement, and helping both parties work together as the case progresses. We hold ourselves to an incredibly high bar, because we know it results in life-changing aid for those in need.  A few examples of what we’re currently working on:\n\n - Improve an existing framework to match clients to the best law firm in our network available (for their case, geography, client and firm preferences, etc.) and work with the Data Science team to turn it into a reality.\n\n - Interview partner law firms to prioritize the next set of features we’ll build, then partner with Design and Engineering to craft a formal roadmap and mock up wireframes for our next product launch.\n\n - Leverage data from our call center and case details to optimize how and when we reach clients across mediums and throughout their case lifecycle.\n\n - Build a core data platform to support multiple verticals at varying scales with model-driven decision making and personalization throughout the funnel.\n\n\nRESPONSIBILITIES\n\n - Get to know our users - both clients and lawyers - and understand their needs.\n\n - Craft a product vision for our next phase of growth. Go deep on strategy: become an expert in our business model, current offering, and key milestones to inform your work.\n\n - Develop a comprehensive product roadmap and build alignment for it with stakeholders and senior leadership.\n\n - Work with engineering and design to build and ship new products and features. Play the role of conductor, coordinating and empowering others.\n\n - Own key targets and metrics. Collect and analyze data, and use it to drive decision-making at a company level. Propose hypotheses, run experiments, and iterate quickly.\n\n\nQUALIFICATIONS\n\n - 3+ years of product management experience, building and shipping products at scale\n\n - Demonstrated success in setting a product vision and strategy, and the ability to speak thoughtfully about the key decisions and tradeoffs you made\n\n - Knowledge of best practices (from past work in a high-performing organization) and the ability to instill a great product culture as we grow\n\n - Great communication and people skills — shown by great reviews from PMs, engineers and designers you’ve worked with\n\n - Mastery of data platforms and ability to do your own analysis\n\n - A demonstrated commitment to doing good and helping people\n\n - Bonus: Early-stage startup experience - complex consumer business, two-sided marketplace, and/or B2B product\n\n\nSALARY AND BENEFITS\n\nThis is a rare opportunity to join a startup that has strong traction (substantial funding, well-respected backers, tremendous growth, and many happy customers) but is still small enough that you can have a huge impact and play a role in shaping our culture.We’re a certified B Corporation tackling a critical social problem. Our mission to help people in need drives everything we do, and your work here will touch many lives.\n\nWe offer competitive pay — including equity for all employees — and generous benefits:\n\n - Medical and dental insurance with 100% of premiums covered for employees and their families\n\n - 15 vacation days & ~20 paid holidays each year (including two weeks at end-of-year)\n\n - Free membership to OneMedical\n\n - $600/year internet stipend\n\n - $1,000/year reimbursable stipend for education and training outside of work\n\n - Up to $1,200/year student loan repayment assistance\n\n - 401(k) and optional HSA/FSA\n\n - Humble, thoughtful, smart, fun colleagues\n\n\nLOCATION\n\nThis job is fully remote and we’re committed to empowering everyone with flexibility. Work remotely, and travel to LA (on the company dime) as needed to be with your colleagues – usually quarterly, plus offsites. We care a lot about building a great culture and we think some interactions need to happen in person, so we put a lot of thought into retreats, offsites, and other ways to gather.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"a17fec50-5b19-496d-81d1-0a3303011720","title":"Attorney","department":"General","team":"General","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2025-05-12T21:45:47.958+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Los Angeles"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/atticus/a17fec50-5b19-496d-81d1-0a3303011720","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/atticus/a17fec50-5b19-496d-81d1-0a3303011720/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2><strong>About Atticus</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At any given time, 16 million Americans are experiencing a crisis that requires urgent help from our legal system or government. The right assistance could transform their lives. But today, most never get it.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Atticus makes it easy for any sick or injured American to get life-changing aid. Our mission is to tear down barriers between people in crisis and the aid they deserve. In the last six years, we’ve become the leading platform connecting people with disabilities to government benefits.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We also help victims of accidents, misconduct, and violence get compensation from insurance. So far, we’ve helped hundreds of thousands of people access over $10 billion in life-changing aid —and earned over 20,000 five-star reviews. And we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We've raised more than $100 million from top VC firms like Fika, Forerunner, Google Ventures, and True Ventures, and we’re on our way to creating a category defining business assisting needy Americans.</p><h2><strong>The Job</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The core of this job is representing our clients in their pursuit of Social Security Disability benefits. You’ll join a small team of attorneys and paralegals who are advocating for clients to the highest possible standard of representation. You should expect to handle 25-50 clients simultaneously, with only a portion of these active at one time.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role will also provide opportunities to lead or support projects at the intersection of client service and technology, with meaningful proximity to a product/engineering team dedicated to building tools for the next generation of legal practice.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The ideal candidate for this role is both passionate about and skilled in representing clients in poverty, while also possessing a curiosity for how technology and the vehicle of a venture-backed startup can transform outcomes for clients at scale.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role is a unique opportunity to do meaningful social impact work as an attorney in a rapidly scaling startup where we put a premium on work-life balance. Your path from here could include growing as a leader at Atticus or transitioning further into tech/business.</p><h2><strong>Qualifications</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Required:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You excelled in high-volume direct services legal practice or at a top law firm.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You are a resourceful team player ready to dive into a scrappy startup environment where you will learn quickly and get your hands dirty.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You have a demonstrated commitment to doing good and helping people.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You have a degree from a top law school where you demonstrated strong academic performance.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You are admitted to the bar in any state.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bonus / Nice-to-Have:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You have several years of meaningful work experience prior to attending law school, especially in client service or business environments.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You have experience at a startup or other fast-paced, agile environment.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are strongly committed to building a diverse team. If you’re from a background that’s underrepresented in tech, we’d love to meet you.</p><h2><strong>Salary and Benefits</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare opportunity to join a startup that has strong traction (substantial funding, well-respected backers, tremendous growth, and many happy customers) but is still small enough that you can have a huge impact and play a role in shaping our culture.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We’re a certified B Corporation tackling a critical social problem. Our mission to help people in need drives everything we do, and your work here will touch many lives.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We offer competitive pay — including equity for all employees — and generous benefits:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Medical and dental insurance with 100% of premiums covered for employees and their families</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">15 vacation days &amp; ~20 paid holidays each year (including two weeks at end-of-year)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Free membership to OneMedical</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$600/year internet stipend</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$1,000/year reimbursable stipend for education and training outside of work</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Up to $1,200/year student loan repayment assistance</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">401(k) and optional HSA/FSA</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Humble, thoughtful, smart, fun colleagues</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We anticipate the base salary band for this role will be between $140,000 and $175,000 in addition to equity and benefits. The salary at offer will be determined by a number of factors such as candidate’s experience, knowledge, skills and abilities, as well as internal equity among our team.</p><h2><strong>Location</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This job is fully remote and we’re committed to empowering everyone with flexibility. Work remotely, and travel to LA (on the company dime) as needed to be with your colleagues – usually quarterly, plus offsites. We care a lot about building a great culture and we think some interactions need to happen in person, so we put a lot of thought into retreats, offsites, and other ways to gather.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p>","descriptionPlain":"ABOUT ATTICUS\n\nAt any given time, 16 million Americans are experiencing a crisis that requires urgent help from our legal system or government. The right assistance could transform their lives. But today, most never get it.\n\nAtticus makes it easy for any sick or injured American to get life-changing aid. Our mission is to tear down barriers between people in crisis and the aid they deserve. In the last six years, we’ve become the leading platform connecting people with disabilities to government benefits.\n\nWe also help victims of accidents, misconduct, and violence get compensation from insurance. So far, we’ve helped hundreds of thousands of people access over $10 billion in life-changing aid —and earned over 20,000 five-star reviews. And we’re just getting started.\n\nWe've raised more than $100 million from top VC firms like Fika, Forerunner, Google Ventures, and True Ventures, and we’re on our way to creating a category defining business assisting needy Americans.\n\n\nTHE JOB\n\nThe core of this job is representing our clients in their pursuit of Social Security Disability benefits. You’ll join a small team of attorneys and paralegals who are advocating for clients to the highest possible standard of representation. You should expect to handle 25-50 clients simultaneously, with only a portion of these active at one time.\n\nThis role will also provide opportunities to lead or support projects at the intersection of client service and technology, with meaningful proximity to a product/engineering team dedicated to building tools for the next generation of legal practice.\n\nThe ideal candidate for this role is both passionate about and skilled in representing clients in poverty, while also possessing a curiosity for how technology and the vehicle of a venture-backed startup can transform outcomes for clients at scale.\n\nThis role is a unique opportunity to do meaningful social impact work as an attorney in a rapidly scaling startup where we put a premium on work-life balance. Your path from here could include growing as a leader at Atticus or transitioning further into tech/business.\n\n\nQUALIFICATIONS\n\nRequired:\n\n - You excelled in high-volume direct services legal practice or at a top law firm.\n\n - You are a resourceful team player ready to dive into a scrappy startup environment where you will learn quickly and get your hands dirty.\n\n - You have a demonstrated commitment to doing good and helping people.\n\n - You have a degree from a top law school where you demonstrated strong academic performance.\n\n - You are admitted to the bar in any state.\n\nBonus / Nice-to-Have:\n\n - You have several years of meaningful work experience prior to attending law school, especially in client service or business environments.\n\n - You have experience at a startup or other fast-paced, agile environment.\n\nWe are strongly committed to building a diverse team. If you’re from a background that’s underrepresented in tech, we’d love to meet you.\n\n\nSALARY AND BENEFITS\n\nThis is a rare opportunity to join a startup that has strong traction (substantial funding, well-respected backers, tremendous growth, and many happy customers) but is still small enough that you can have a huge impact and play a role in shaping our culture.\n\nWe’re a certified B Corporation tackling a critical social problem. Our mission to help people in need drives everything we do, and your work here will touch many lives.\n\nWe offer competitive pay — including equity for all employees — and generous benefits:\n\n - Medical and dental insurance with 100% of premiums covered for employees and their families\n\n - 15 vacation days & ~20 paid holidays each year (including two weeks at end-of-year)\n\n - Free membership to OneMedical\n\n - $600/year internet stipend\n\n - $1,000/year reimbursable stipend for education and training outside of work\n\n - Up to $1,200/year student loan repayment assistance\n\n - 401(k) and optional HSA/FSA\n\n - Humble, thoughtful, smart, fun colleagues\n\nWe anticipate the base salary band for this role will be between $140,000 and $175,000 in addition to equity and benefits. The salary at offer will be determined by a number of factors such as candidate’s experience, knowledge, skills and abilities, as well as internal equity among our team.\n\n\nLOCATION\n\nThis job is fully remote and we’re committed to empowering everyone with flexibility. Work remotely, and travel to LA (on the company dime) as needed to be with your colleagues – usually quarterly, plus offsites. We care a lot about building a great culture and we think some interactions need to happen in person, so we put a lot of thought into retreats, offsites, and other ways to gather.\n\n","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"e27531ca-47c0-4282-87c3-65e6db4718d0","title":"Lead Infrastructure Engineer","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-01-29T22:48:05.028+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Los Angeles"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/atticus/e27531ca-47c0-4282-87c3-65e6db4718d0","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/atticus/e27531ca-47c0-4282-87c3-65e6db4718d0/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2>About Atticus</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At any given time, 16 million Americans are experiencing a crisis that requires urgent help from our legal system or government. The right assistance could transform their lives. But today, most never get it.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Atticus makes it easy for any sick or injured American to get life-changing aid. Our mission is to tear down barriers between people in crisis and the aid they deserve. In the last six years, we’ve become the leading platform connecting people with disabilities to government benefits.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We also help victims of accidents, misconduct, and violence get compensation from insurance. So far, we’ve helped hundreds of thousands of people access over $10 billion in life-changing aid —and earned over 20,000 five-star reviews. And we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We've raised more than $100 million from top VC firms like Fika, Forerunner, Google Ventures, and True Ventures, and we’re on our way to creating a category defining business assisting needy Americans.</p><h2>The Job</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're looking for a Lead Infrastructure Engineer to define what great infrastructure looks like at Atticus and build the platforms and tooling that help engineers ship fast without breaking things.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You'll be our second infrastructure engineer, working with <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/in/jeremebounds/\"><u>Jereme</u></a> to shape our technical foundations from the ground up — setting the vision, building the systems, and establishing the practices that will support Atticus for years to come.</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You'll own infrastructure as a product</strong>, serving Atticus's product engineering teams as your customers. This means:</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Shaping our infrastructure roadmap</strong> — developing a clear vision for where our infra needs to go and driving progress toward it</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Building security and operational foundations</strong> — laying the groundwork for sustainable growth</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Improving reliability</strong> — reducing MTTR, establishing SLOs, bringing rigor to how we manage outages</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Empowering product teams</strong> — you'll build the platforms and tools that let them own their systems end-to-end</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a senior IC role reporting directly to <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/in/twaite/\"><u>Toby, our VP of Engineering</u></a>. You'll have a major hand in shaping our infrastructure strategy — and you'll also be writing code and shipping directly. We're a 20-person engineering team, so there's no layer of abstraction between you and the work.</p><h2>Qualifications</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Required:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>5+ years in infrastructure / SRE / platform engineering roles</strong>, with breadth across infra disciplines. We're looking for an infra generalist, not a deep specialist in one narrow area.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Hands-on experience with cloud infrastructure</strong> (GCP preferred) and infrastructure-as-code tools (Terraform, Pulumi, etc.)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Strong software engineering fundamentals.</strong> You approach infrastructure with a builder's mindset.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Technical breadth across infra domains:</strong> networking, security, observability, CI/CD, database operations, containerization. We don’t expect you to be an expert in everything, just knowledgeable enough to be effective on a small team without other specialists.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Experience with consumer-facing, revenue-critical systems</strong>, though you don't need FAANG-scale experience.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bonus / Nice-to-Have:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You've led infrastructure evolution at a growing startup</strong>, not just maintained existing systems. Ideally on a small team (&lt;5 infra engineers).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You're excited by environments with little structure</strong> — where you're expected to understand the bigger picture, cut through ambiguity, and figure out what matters most.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are strongly committed to building a diverse team. If you're from a background that's underrepresented in tech, we'd love to meet you.</p><h2>Salary and Benefits</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare opportunity to join a startup that has strong traction (substantial funding, well-respected backers, tremendous growth, and many happy customers) but is still small enough that you can have a huge impact and play a role in shaping our culture.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're a certified B Corporation tackling a critical social problem. Our mission to help people in need drives everything we do, and your work here will touch many lives.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We offer competitive pay — including equity for all employees — and generous benefits:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Medical and dental insurance with 100% of premiums covered for employees and their families</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">15 vacation days &amp; ~20 paid holidays each year (including two weeks at the end-of-year)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Free membership to OneMedical</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$600/year internet stipend</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$1,000/year reimbursable stipend for education and training outside of work</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Up to $1,200/year student loan repayment assistance</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">401(k) and optional HSA/FSA</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Humble, thoughtful, smart, fun colleagues</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We anticipate the base salary band for this role will be between $170,000 and $220,000 in addition to equity and benefits. The salary at offer will be determined by a number of factors such as candidate's experience, knowledge, skills and abilities, as well as internal equity among our team.</p><h2>Location</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This job is fully remote and we're committed to empowering everyone with flexibility. Work remotely, and travel to LA (on the company dime) as needed to be with your colleagues — usually quarterly, plus offsites. We care a lot about building a great culture and we think some interactions need to happen in person, so we put a lot of thought into retreats, offsites, and other ways to gather.</p>","descriptionPlain":"ABOUT ATTICUS\n\nAt any given time, 16 million Americans are experiencing a crisis that requires urgent help from our legal system or government. The right assistance could transform their lives. But today, most never get it.\n\nAtticus makes it easy for any sick or injured American to get life-changing aid. Our mission is to tear down barriers between people in crisis and the aid they deserve. In the last six years, we’ve become the leading platform connecting people with disabilities to government benefits.\n\nWe also help victims of accidents, misconduct, and violence get compensation from insurance. So far, we’ve helped hundreds of thousands of people access over $10 billion in life-changing aid —and earned over 20,000 five-star reviews. And we’re just getting started.\n\nWe've raised more than $100 million from top VC firms like Fika, Forerunner, Google Ventures, and True Ventures, and we’re on our way to creating a category defining business assisting needy Americans.\n\n\nTHE JOB\n\nWe're looking for a Lead Infrastructure Engineer to define what great infrastructure looks like at Atticus and build the platforms and tooling that help engineers ship fast without breaking things.\n\nYou'll be our second infrastructure engineer, working with Jereme https://www.linkedin.com/in/jeremebounds/ to shape our technical foundations from the ground up — setting the vision, building the systems, and establishing the practices that will support Atticus for years to come.\n\n - You'll own infrastructure as a product, serving Atticus's product engineering teams as your customers. This means:\n\n - Shaping our infrastructure roadmap — developing a clear vision for where our infra needs to go and driving progress toward it\n\n - Building security and operational foundations — laying the groundwork for sustainable growth\n\n - Improving reliability — reducing MTTR, establishing SLOs, bringing rigor to how we manage outages\n\n - Empowering product teams — you'll build the platforms and tools that let them own their systems end-to-end\n\nThis is a senior IC role reporting directly to Toby, our VP of Engineering https://www.linkedin.com/in/twaite/. You'll have a major hand in shaping our infrastructure strategy — and you'll also be writing code and shipping directly. We're a 20-person engineering team, so there's no layer of abstraction between you and the work.\n\n\nQUALIFICATIONS\n\nRequired:\n\n - 5+ years in infrastructure / SRE / platform engineering roles, with breadth across infra disciplines. We're looking for an infra generalist, not a deep specialist in one narrow area.\n\n - Hands-on experience with cloud infrastructure (GCP preferred) and infrastructure-as-code tools (Terraform, Pulumi, etc.)\n\n - Strong software engineering fundamentals. You approach infrastructure with a builder's mindset.\n\n - Technical breadth across infra domains: networking, security, observability, CI/CD, database operations, containerization. We don’t expect you to be an expert in everything, just knowledgeable enough to be effective on a small team without other specialists.\n\n - Experience with consumer-facing, revenue-critical systems, though you don't need FAANG-scale experience.\n\nBonus / Nice-to-Have:\n\n - You've led infrastructure evolution at a growing startup, not just maintained existing systems. Ideally on a small team (<5 infra engineers).\n\n - You're excited by environments with little structure — where you're expected to understand the bigger picture, cut through ambiguity, and figure out what matters most.\n\nWe are strongly committed to building a diverse team. If you're from a background that's underrepresented in tech, we'd love to meet you.\n\n\nSALARY AND BENEFITS\n\nThis is a rare opportunity to join a startup that has strong traction (substantial funding, well-respected backers, tremendous growth, and many happy customers) but is still small enough that you can have a huge impact and play a role in shaping our culture.\n\nWe're a certified B Corporation tackling a critical social problem. Our mission to help people in need drives everything we do, and your work here will touch many lives.\n\nWe offer competitive pay — including equity for all employees — and generous benefits:\n\n - Medical and dental insurance with 100% of premiums covered for employees and their families\n\n - 15 vacation days & ~20 paid holidays each year (including two weeks at the end-of-year)\n\n - Free membership to OneMedical\n\n - $600/year internet stipend\n\n - $1,000/year reimbursable stipend for education and training outside of work\n\n - Up to $1,200/year student loan repayment assistance\n\n - 401(k) and optional HSA/FSA\n\n - Humble, thoughtful, smart, fun colleagues\n\nWe anticipate the base salary band for this role will be between $170,000 and $220,000 in addition to equity and benefits. The salary at offer will be determined by a number of factors such as candidate's experience, knowledge, skills and abilities, as well as internal equity among our team.\n\n\nLOCATION\n\nThis job is fully remote and we're committed to empowering everyone with flexibility. Work remotely, and travel to LA (on the company dime) as needed to be with your colleagues — usually quarterly, plus offsites. We care a lot about building a great culture and we think some interactions need to happen in person, so we put a lot of thought into retreats, offsites, and other ways to gather.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"7663356d-e896-48d0-b884-1fe685c2509e","title":"Senior Backend Engineer - Representation","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-03-30T21:58:04.353+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Los Angeles"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/atticus/7663356d-e896-48d0-b884-1fe685c2509e","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/atticus/7663356d-e896-48d0-b884-1fe685c2509e/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2><strong>About Atticus</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At any given time, 16 million Americans are experiencing a crisis that requires urgent help from our legal system or government. The right assistance could transform their lives. But today, most never get it.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Atticus makes it easy for any sick or injured American to get life-changing aid. Our mission is to tear down barriers between people in crisis and the aid they deserve. In the last six years, we’ve become the leading platform connecting people with disabilities to government benefits.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We also help victims of accidents, misconduct, and violence get compensation from insurance. So far, we’ve helped hundreds of thousands of people access over $10 billion in life-changing aid —and earned over 20,000 five-star reviews. And we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We've raised more than $100 million from top VC firms like Fika, Forerunner, Google Ventures, and True Ventures, and we’re on our way to creating a category defining business assisting needy Americans.</p><h2><strong>The Job</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Atticus works in an industry dominated by outdated technology that is ripe for fresh thinking. Our core competitors rely on massive call centers, antiquated CRMs, and paper checks. As a VC-backed tech company, our engineering team powers everything we do — from creating elegant and intuitive product experiences for people in crisis who are seeking legal aid, to building powerful tools for our network of attorneys that actually help them win the benefits they need.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're looking for a backend-leaning senior software engineer to join our Representation Pod, a cross-functional team of engineers, PMs, and designers building the core tools that help the law firms in our network deliver consistent and effective representation for our clients. The Rep Pod is building new products from scratch: reimagining what legal experiences for our clients and attorneys with today’s technology.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a senior individual contributor role. You'll own complex backend challenges around how we structure data, systems, and APIs — while staying deeply connected to the clients &amp; lawyers who use the products you build. That means bringing both genuine user empathy and sharp product instincts alongside the technical depth to make hard architectural decisions and see them through.</p><h2><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own significant backend systems end-to-end: set and hold a high bar for architecture, design, implementation, and production health.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner closely with product and design to shape requirements, not just implement them — we trust your intuitions and want you to have opinions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You’ll bring 0-to-1 product thinking to an area where your work has a tangible impact on our client’s wellbeing.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Mentor engineers on the team, with particular emphasis on backend patterns</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work across the stack as needed, everything from frontend UI work to data systems.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>What We're Looking For</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Required:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5+ years of experience building production software, including meaningful time at a seed-stage startup or as an early member of a new product team at a later-stage company — with clear evidence of increasing scope and ownership over time</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience on a high-performing product team, working closely with strong PMs and designers to ship user-focused solutions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience designing and operating reliable, scalable backend systems and APIs, with a high bar for data modeling and architecture</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep user empathy — you think carefully about the people using what you build, not just the technical implementation</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A track record of mentoring engineers and genuine excitement about helping teammates grow</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bonus / Nice to Have:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with Go</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with Google Cloud Platform, Kubernetes, Terraform, &amp; Docker</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Background in industries with complex workflows — legal, healthcare, or financial services</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience building products for consumers or two-sided marketplaces</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience evolving systems as teams and traffic scale</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Interest in developer experience, internal tooling, or team process improvement</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are strongly committed to building a diverse team. If you're from a background that's underrepresented in tech, we'd love to meet you.</p><h2><strong>Salary and Benefits</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare opportunity to join a startup with strong traction — substantial funding, well-respected backers, real growth, and thousands of happy customers — while still being small enough to have a huge impact and help shape our culture.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're a certified B Corporation tackling a critical social problem. Everything we build touches real lives.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We offer competitive pay — including equity for all employees — and generous benefits:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Medical and dental insurance with 100% of premiums covered for employees and their families</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">15 vacation days and ~20 paid holidays per year, including two weeks at end-of-year</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Free OneMedical membership</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$600/year internet stipend</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$1,000/year education and training reimbursement</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Up to $1,200/year student loan repayment assistance</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">401(k) and optional HSA/FSA</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Base salary range: $157,250 to $230,000, plus equity and benefits. Offer will reflect candidate experience, skills, and internal equity.</p><h2><strong>Location</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This job is fully remote and we’re committed to empowering everyone with flexibility. Work remotely, and travel to LA (on the company dime) as needed to be with your colleagues —somewhere between quarterly and yearly. We care a lot about building a great culture and we think some interactions need to happen in person, so we put a lot of thought into retreats, offsites, and other ways to gather.</p>","descriptionPlain":"ABOUT ATTICUS\n\nAt any given time, 16 million Americans are experiencing a crisis that requires urgent help from our legal system or government. The right assistance could transform their lives. But today, most never get it.\n\nAtticus makes it easy for any sick or injured American to get life-changing aid. Our mission is to tear down barriers between people in crisis and the aid they deserve. In the last six years, we’ve become the leading platform connecting people with disabilities to government benefits.\n\nWe also help victims of accidents, misconduct, and violence get compensation from insurance. So far, we’ve helped hundreds of thousands of people access over $10 billion in life-changing aid —and earned over 20,000 five-star reviews. And we’re just getting started.\n\nWe've raised more than $100 million from top VC firms like Fika, Forerunner, Google Ventures, and True Ventures, and we’re on our way to creating a category defining business assisting needy Americans.\n\n\nTHE JOB\n\nAtticus works in an industry dominated by outdated technology that is ripe for fresh thinking. Our core competitors rely on massive call centers, antiquated CRMs, and paper checks. As a VC-backed tech company, our engineering team powers everything we do — from creating elegant and intuitive product experiences for people in crisis who are seeking legal aid, to building powerful tools for our network of attorneys that actually help them win the benefits they need.\n\nWe're looking for a backend-leaning senior software engineer to join our Representation Pod, a cross-functional team of engineers, PMs, and designers building the core tools that help the law firms in our network deliver consistent and effective representation for our clients. The Rep Pod is building new products from scratch: reimagining what legal experiences for our clients and attorneys with today’s technology.\n\nThis is a senior individual contributor role. You'll own complex backend challenges around how we structure data, systems, and APIs — while staying deeply connected to the clients & lawyers who use the products you build. That means bringing both genuine user empathy and sharp product instincts alongside the technical depth to make hard architectural decisions and see them through.\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Own significant backend systems end-to-end: set and hold a high bar for architecture, design, implementation, and production health.\n\n - Partner closely with product and design to shape requirements, not just implement them — we trust your intuitions and want you to have opinions\n\n - You’ll bring 0-to-1 product thinking to an area where your work has a tangible impact on our client’s wellbeing.\n\n - Mentor engineers on the team, with particular emphasis on backend patterns\n\n - Work across the stack as needed, everything from frontend UI work to data systems.\n\n\nWHAT WE'RE LOOKING FOR\n\nRequired:\n\n - 5+ years of experience building production software, including meaningful time at a seed-stage startup or as an early member of a new product team at a later-stage company — with clear evidence of increasing scope and ownership over time\n\n - Experience on a high-performing product team, working closely with strong PMs and designers to ship user-focused solutions\n\n - Experience designing and operating reliable, scalable backend systems and APIs, with a high bar for data modeling and architecture\n\n - Deep user empathy — you think carefully about the people using what you build, not just the technical implementation\n\n - A track record of mentoring engineers and genuine excitement about helping teammates grow\n\nBonus / Nice to Have:\n\n - Experience with Go\n\n - Experience with Google Cloud Platform, Kubernetes, Terraform, & Docker\n\n - Background in industries with complex workflows — legal, healthcare, or financial services\n\n - Experience building products for consumers or two-sided marketplaces\n\n - Experience evolving systems as teams and traffic scale\n\n - Interest in developer experience, internal tooling, or team process improvement\n\nWe are strongly committed to building a diverse team. If you're from a background that's underrepresented in tech, we'd love to meet you.\n\n\nSALARY AND BENEFITS\n\nThis is a rare opportunity to join a startup with strong traction — substantial funding, well-respected backers, real growth, and thousands of happy customers — while still being small enough to have a huge impact and help shape our culture.\n\nWe're a certified B Corporation tackling a critical social problem. Everything we build touches real lives.\n\nWe offer competitive pay — including equity for all employees — and generous benefits:\n\n - Medical and dental insurance with 100% of premiums covered for employees and their families\n\n - 15 vacation days and ~20 paid holidays per year, including two weeks at end-of-year\n\n - Free OneMedical membership\n\n - $600/year internet stipend\n\n - $1,000/year education and training reimbursement\n\n - Up to $1,200/year student loan repayment assistance\n\n - 401(k) and optional HSA/FSA\n\nBase salary range: $157,250 to $230,000, plus equity and benefits. Offer will reflect candidate experience, skills, and internal equity.\n\n\nLOCATION\n\nThis job is fully remote and we’re committed to empowering everyone with flexibility. Work remotely, and travel to LA (on the company dime) as needed to be with your colleagues —somewhere between quarterly and yearly. We care a lot about building a great culture and we think some interactions need to happen in person, so we put a lot of thought into retreats, offsites, and other ways to gather.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"299af7cf-5963-43a9-8262-be4358271358","title":"Lead Data Engineer","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-27T16:27:33.585+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Los Angeles"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/atticus/299af7cf-5963-43a9-8262-be4358271358","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/atticus/299af7cf-5963-43a9-8262-be4358271358/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2><strong>About Atticus</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At any given time, 16 million Americans are experiencing a crisis that requires urgent help from our legal system or government. The right assistance could transform their lives. But today, most never get it.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Atticus makes it easy for any sick or injured American to get life-changing aid. Our mission is to tear down barriers between people in crisis and the aid they deserve. In the last six years, we’ve become the leading platform connecting people with disabilities to government benefits.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We also help victims of accidents, misconduct, and violence get compensation from insurance. So far, we’ve helped hundreds of thousands of people access over $10 billion in life-changing aid —and earned over 20,000 five-star reviews. And we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We've raised more than $100 million from top VC firms like Fika, Forerunner, Google Ventures, and True Ventures, and we’re on our way to creating a category defining business assisting needy Americans.</p><h2><strong>The Job</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are looking for our first in-house Data Engineer to own and evolve our core data infrastructure. This is an early and high-impact role. As the data engineering function grows under Engineering, you'll have a real voice in shaping how it's built - the processes, standards, and team culture.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You'll sit at the intersection of our Engineering and Business Operations teams, which means you'll spend your time both building reliable, scalable systems and translating business needs into well-designed data products. You'll work closely with data scientists, business analysts, and product leaders to make sure our data is clean, accessible, and trustworthy.</p><h2><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own and operate our data warehouse, pipelines, and transformation layer</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design, build, and maintain scalable, reliable data pipelines that ingest data from across our platform and third-party sources, ensuring data is always available and trustworthy for downstream consumers</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner with data scientists and analysts to deliver clean, well-documented datasets and optimize query performance so teams spend less time wrangling data and more time generating insights</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Incrementally improve and modernize our existing data systems - you won't build everything from scratch, but you'll know how to assess what we have, prioritize what matters, and migrate thoughtfully</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Implement data quality monitoring, alerting, and documentation practices that build trust across the organization</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The role is a rare opportunity to join a fast-growing Series C startup that doubles as a B-corp social enterprise. Every project you take on will help clients in need get the help they deserve, and you’ll shape our company culture as we scale. We’re looking for data scientists who are excited about our mission and the challenges it entails.</p><h2><strong>Qualifications</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Required:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">4+ years of professional experience in data engineering, ideally at a high-growth startup or fast-moving team within a larger organization</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hands-on experience with the modern data stack - proficiency with BigQuery (or a comparable cloud warehouse), dbt, and an orchestration tool like Dagster or Airflow</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong SQL skills and fluency in Golang, Python, or another common Data Engineering language</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Track record of improving or modernizing data systems iteratively - you're comfortable inheriting legacy infrastructure and systems and making them progressively better</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong communication and collaboration skills - able to work fluidly across both technical and business-oriented teams</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bonus / Nice-to-Have:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience transitioning data infrastructure from an outsourced or contractor model to an in-house team</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with data observability tools</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience supporting or collaborating with a data science function, including ML feature pipelines</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are strongly committed to building a diverse team. If you’re from a background that’s underrepresented in tech, we’d love to meet you.</p><h2><strong>Salary and Benefits</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare opportunity to join a startup that has strong traction (substantial funding, well-respected backers, tremendous growth, and many happy customers) but is still small enough that you can have a huge impact and play a role in shaping our culture.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're a certified B Corporation tackling a critical social problem. Our mission to help people in need drives everything we do, and your work here will touch many lives.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We offer competitive pay—including equity for all employees —and generous benefits:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Medical and dental insurance with 100% of premiums covered for employees and their families</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">15 vacation days &amp; ~20 paid holidays each year (including two weeks at end-of-year)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Free membership to OneMedical</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$600/year internet stipend</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$1,000/year reimbursable stipend for education and training outside of work</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Up to $1,200/year student loan repayment assistance</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">401(k) and optional HSA/FSA</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We anticipate the base salary band for this role will be between $174,000 and $230,000 in addition to equity and benefits. The salary at offer will be determined by a number of factors such as candidate's experience, knowledge, skills and abilities, as well as internal equity among our team.</p><h2><strong>Location</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This job is fully remote and we're committed to empowering everyone with flexibility. Work remotely, and travel to LA (on the company dime) as needed to be with your colleagues – usually quarterly, plus offsites. We care a lot about building a great culture and we think some interactions need to happen in person, so we put a lot of thought into retreats, offsites, and other ways to gather.</p>","descriptionPlain":"ABOUT ATTICUS\n\nAt any given time, 16 million Americans are experiencing a crisis that requires urgent help from our legal system or government. The right assistance could transform their lives. But today, most never get it.\n\nAtticus makes it easy for any sick or injured American to get life-changing aid. Our mission is to tear down barriers between people in crisis and the aid they deserve. In the last six years, we’ve become the leading platform connecting people with disabilities to government benefits.\n\nWe also help victims of accidents, misconduct, and violence get compensation from insurance. So far, we’ve helped hundreds of thousands of people access over $10 billion in life-changing aid —and earned over 20,000 five-star reviews. And we’re just getting started.\n\nWe've raised more than $100 million from top VC firms like Fika, Forerunner, Google Ventures, and True Ventures, and we’re on our way to creating a category defining business assisting needy Americans.\n\n\nTHE JOB\n\nWe are looking for our first in-house Data Engineer to own and evolve our core data infrastructure. This is an early and high-impact role. As the data engineering function grows under Engineering, you'll have a real voice in shaping how it's built - the processes, standards, and team culture.\n\nYou'll sit at the intersection of our Engineering and Business Operations teams, which means you'll spend your time both building reliable, scalable systems and translating business needs into well-designed data products. You'll work closely with data scientists, business analysts, and product leaders to make sure our data is clean, accessible, and trustworthy.\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Own and operate our data warehouse, pipelines, and transformation layer\n\n - Design, build, and maintain scalable, reliable data pipelines that ingest data from across our platform and third-party sources, ensuring data is always available and trustworthy for downstream consumers\n\n - Partner with data scientists and analysts to deliver clean, well-documented datasets and optimize query performance so teams spend less time wrangling data and more time generating insights\n\n - Incrementally improve and modernize our existing data systems - you won't build everything from scratch, but you'll know how to assess what we have, prioritize what matters, and migrate thoughtfully\n\n - Implement data quality monitoring, alerting, and documentation practices that build trust across the organization\n\nThe role is a rare opportunity to join a fast-growing Series C startup that doubles as a B-corp social enterprise. Every project you take on will help clients in need get the help they deserve, and you’ll shape our company culture as we scale. We’re looking for data scientists who are excited about our mission and the challenges it entails.\n\n\nQUALIFICATIONS\n\nRequired:\n\n - 4+ years of professional experience in data engineering, ideally at a high-growth startup or fast-moving team within a larger organization\n\n - Hands-on experience with the modern data stack - proficiency with BigQuery (or a comparable cloud warehouse), dbt, and an orchestration tool like Dagster or Airflow\n\n - Strong SQL skills and fluency in Golang, Python, or another common Data Engineering language\n\n - Track record of improving or modernizing data systems iteratively - you're comfortable inheriting legacy infrastructure and systems and making them progressively better\n\n - Strong communication and collaboration skills - able to work fluidly across both technical and business-oriented teams\n\nBonus / Nice-to-Have:\n\n - Experience transitioning data infrastructure from an outsourced or contractor model to an in-house team\n\n - Familiarity with data observability tools\n\n - Experience supporting or collaborating with a data science function, including ML feature pipelines\n\nWe are strongly committed to building a diverse team. If you’re from a background that’s underrepresented in tech, we’d love to meet you.\n\n\nSALARY AND BENEFITS\n\nThis is a rare opportunity to join a startup that has strong traction (substantial funding, well-respected backers, tremendous growth, and many happy customers) but is still small enough that you can have a huge impact and play a role in shaping our culture.\n\nWe're a certified B Corporation tackling a critical social problem. Our mission to help people in need drives everything we do, and your work here will touch many lives.\n\nWe offer competitive pay—including equity for all employees —and generous benefits:\n\n - Medical and dental insurance with 100% of premiums covered for employees and their families\n\n - 15 vacation days & ~20 paid holidays each year (including two weeks at end-of-year)\n\n - Free membership to OneMedical\n\n - $600/year internet stipend\n\n - $1,000/year reimbursable stipend for education and training outside of work\n\n - Up to $1,200/year student loan repayment assistance\n\n - 401(k) and optional HSA/FSA\n\nWe anticipate the base salary band for this role will be between $174,000 and $230,000 in addition to equity and benefits. The salary at offer will be determined by a number of factors such as candidate's experience, knowledge, skills and abilities, as well as internal equity among our team.\n\n\nLOCATION\n\nThis job is fully remote and we're committed to empowering everyone with flexibility. Work remotely, and travel to LA (on the company dime) as needed to be with your colleagues – usually quarterly, plus offsites. We care a lot about building a great culture and we think some interactions need to happen in person, so we put a lot of thought into retreats, offsites, and other ways to gather.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"d18fd075-a88f-4197-a718-9020b4a727b8","title":"People Operations Manager","department":"People","team":"People","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-09T18:26:14.834+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Los Angeles"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/atticus/d18fd075-a88f-4197-a718-9020b4a727b8","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/atticus/d18fd075-a88f-4197-a718-9020b4a727b8/application","descriptionHtml":"<h1></h1><h2><strong>About Atticus</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At any given time, 16 million Americans are experiencing a crisis that requires urgent help from our legal system or government. The right assistance could transform their lives. But today, most never get it.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Atticus makes it easy for any sick or injured American to get life-changing aid. Our mission is to tear down barriers between people in crisis and the aid they deserve. In the last six years, we’ve become the leading platform connecting people with disabilities to government benefits.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We also help victims of accidents, misconduct, and violence get compensation from insurance. So far, we’ve helped hundreds of thousands of people access over $10 billion in life-changing aid —and earned over 20,000 five-star reviews. And we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We've raised more than $100 million from top VC firms like Fika, Forerunner, Google Ventures, and True Ventures, and we’re on our way to creating a category defining business assisting needy Americans.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>The Job</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">In the next two years, we aim to help over 250,000 Americans get access to life changing benefits. Our People team is core to that goal; to make it happen, we’ll need a values-driven and high-performing organization where great work gets done.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We’re looking for a People Operations leader to join us. This individual contributor role will sit at the center of how we hire, onboard, and support our people, with ownership over the systems and processes that make Atticus a great place to work. You’ll help define our benefits offerings as we evolve, streamline our people technology and processes, and improve our employee experience. You'll report directly to the Head of People and join a small, high-ownership team that cares deeply about our mission and having tangible impact.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>What You’ll Do</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own core people operations areas: onboarding, offboarding, policy / leave administration, benefits, payroll, and compliance</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage benefits end-to-end — employee support, leave management, lead open enrollment, manage vendor relationships, and benchmarking to keep our offerings competitive.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and execute our HRIS operations so that personnel information is always updated; manage our current system, evaluate options, and own HRIS migration when the time comes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Own our PEO relationship, managing the day-to-day relationship and ensuring smooth payroll and compliance across all states.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Manage people reporting and data (headcount, attrition and more) to help our team and stakeholders make good decisions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Evolve our people policies to be current, accessible and useful, and be a resource for managers navigating benefits, people policy, leave and HR system questions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hold a high bar for operational excellence — employees get answers quickly, processes work, and information is clear and accessible.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Qualifications</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">5+ years in People Operations or HR Operations, ideally at a Series B-D startup</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with HRIS systems and PEOs; migration experience is a plus</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Solid grasp of multi-state employment compliance</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Builder's mindset – you delight in improving messy process to get to better outcomes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Low ego, high ownership — you're comfortable doing the work and not just directing it</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable operating in the gray — we believe in low(er) process and high judgment, so we don't have rigid policies for every case. This role requires applying good judgment and care when the answer isn't obvious.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Salary and Benefits</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The role is a rare opportunity to join a fast-growing Series C startup that doubles as a B-corp social enterprise. Our team is still small enough for you to have an outsized impact on how we operate and how our people experience unfolds.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We offer competitive pay — including equity — and generous benefits:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Medical and dental insurance with 100% of employee and family premiums covered</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">15 vacation days &amp; ~20 paid holidays each year (including two weeks at end-of-year)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Free membership to OneMedical</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$600/year internet stipend</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$1,000 reimbursable stipend for education and training outside of work</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Up to $1,200/year student loan repayment assistance</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">401(k) and optional HSA/FSA</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Humble, thoughtful, smart, fun colleagues</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We anticipate the base salary band for this role will be between $130,000 to $160,000 in addition to equity and benefits. The salary at offer will be determined by a number of factors such as candidate’s experience, knowledge, skills and abilities, as well as internal equity among our team.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>Location</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This job is fully remote and we’re committed to empowering everyone with flexibility. Work remotely, and travel to LA (on the company dime) as needed to be with your colleagues – usually quarterly, plus offsites. We care a lot about building a great culture and we think some interactions need to happen in person, so we put a lot of thought into retreats, offsites, and other ways to gather.</p>","descriptionPlain":"ABOUT ATTICUS\n\nAt any given time, 16 million Americans are experiencing a crisis that requires urgent help from our legal system or government. The right assistance could transform their lives. But today, most never get it.\n\nAtticus makes it easy for any sick or injured American to get life-changing aid. Our mission is to tear down barriers between people in crisis and the aid they deserve. In the last six years, we’ve become the leading platform connecting people with disabilities to government benefits.\n\nWe also help victims of accidents, misconduct, and violence get compensation from insurance. So far, we’ve helped hundreds of thousands of people access over $10 billion in life-changing aid —and earned over 20,000 five-star reviews. And we’re just getting started.\n\nWe've raised more than $100 million from top VC firms like Fika, Forerunner, Google Ventures, and True Ventures, and we’re on our way to creating a category defining business assisting needy Americans.\n\n\n\n\nTHE JOB\n\nIn the next two years, we aim to help over 250,000 Americans get access to life changing benefits. Our People team is core to that goal; to make it happen, we’ll need a values-driven and high-performing organization where great work gets done.\n\nWe’re looking for a People Operations leader to join us. This individual contributor role will sit at the center of how we hire, onboard, and support our people, with ownership over the systems and processes that make Atticus a great place to work. You’ll help define our benefits offerings as we evolve, streamline our people technology and processes, and improve our employee experience. You'll report directly to the Head of People and join a small, high-ownership team that cares deeply about our mission and having tangible impact.\n\n\n\nWhat You’ll Do\n\n - Own core people operations areas: onboarding, offboarding, policy / leave administration, benefits, payroll, and compliance\n\n - Manage benefits end-to-end — employee support, leave management, lead open enrollment, manage vendor relationships, and benchmarking to keep our offerings competitive.\n\n - Design and execute our HRIS operations so that personnel information is always updated; manage our current system, evaluate options, and own HRIS migration when the time comes.\n\n - Own our PEO relationship, managing the day-to-day relationship and ensuring smooth payroll and compliance across all states.\n\n - Manage people reporting and data (headcount, attrition and more) to help our team and stakeholders make good decisions.\n\n - Evolve our people policies to be current, accessible and useful, and be a resource for managers navigating benefits, people policy, leave and HR system questions\n\n - Hold a high bar for operational excellence — employees get answers quickly, processes work, and information is clear and accessible.\n\n\nQUALIFICATIONS\n\n - 5+ years in People Operations or HR Operations, ideally at a Series B-D startup\n\n - Experience with HRIS systems and PEOs; migration experience is a plus\n\n - Solid grasp of multi-state employment compliance\n\n - Builder's mindset – you delight in improving messy process to get to better outcomes\n\n - Low ego, high ownership — you're comfortable doing the work and not just directing it\n\n - Comfortable operating in the gray — we believe in low(er) process and high judgment, so we don't have rigid policies for every case. This role requires applying good judgment and care when the answer isn't obvious.\n\n\nSALARY AND BENEFITS\n\nThe role is a rare opportunity to join a fast-growing Series C startup that doubles as a B-corp social enterprise. Our team is still small enough for you to have an outsized impact on how we operate and how our people experience unfolds.\n\nWe offer competitive pay — including equity — and generous benefits:\n\n - Medical and dental insurance with 100% of employee and family premiums covered\n\n - 15 vacation days & ~20 paid holidays each year (including two weeks at end-of-year)\n\n - Free membership to OneMedical\n\n - $600/year internet stipend\n\n - $1,000 reimbursable stipend for education and training outside of work\n\n - Up to $1,200/year student loan repayment assistance\n\n - 401(k) and optional HSA/FSA\n\n - Humble, thoughtful, smart, fun colleagues\n\nWe anticipate the base salary band for this role will be between $130,000 to $160,000 in addition to equity and benefits. The salary at offer will be determined by a number of factors such as candidate’s experience, knowledge, skills and abilities, as well as internal equity among our team.\n\n\n\n\nLOCATION\n\nThis job is fully remote and we’re committed to empowering everyone with flexibility. Work remotely, and travel to LA (on the company dime) as needed to be with your colleagues – usually quarterly, plus offsites. We care a lot about building a great culture and we think some interactions need to happen in person, so we put a lot of thought into retreats, offsites, and other ways to gather.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"d9d7ffcf-24ca-4308-a286-f3d0d7ef5fdf","title":"Head of Web and Organic Growth","department":"Marketing","team":"Marketing","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-22T16:44:21.503+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Los Angeles"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/atticus/d9d7ffcf-24ca-4308-a286-f3d0d7ef5fdf","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/atticus/d9d7ffcf-24ca-4308-a286-f3d0d7ef5fdf/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2><strong>About Atticus</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At any given time, 16 million Americans are experiencing a serious injury or illness that requires urgent help from the legal system or the government. For many, it’s not just a health crisis – it’s the start of a bureaucratic nightmare. The right help could change their lives, but many never get it.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Atticus exists to change that.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're a new kind of law firm that helps sick, injured, and wronged Americans access the benefits designed to protect them — from Social Security disability insurance to workers' comp to insurance settlements. In six years, we've helped hundreds of thousands of people access more than $10 billion in life-changing aid, but our work is far from complete.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We've raised over $100 million from Fika, Forerunner, GV, and True Ventures. We closed our Series C in April 2025, so we're well-funded and investing in growth.</p><h2><br />About the role</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As the Head of Web and Organic Growth, you'll own our digital front door, including the homepage, vertical landing pages, our blog, and lead-magnets. You'll set the strategy to bring prospective clients to <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://Atticus.com\"><u>Atticus.com</u></a> from organic and AI search. You’ll decide what they read, what they trust, and how they move from learning about Atticus to talking with one of our client advocates. You'll write the briefs that shape our blog content and the requirements that drive our SEO and GEO prominence. You'll work closely with our editorial team to commission content that ranks and genuinely helps people in need.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a high-leverage seat. Our prospective clients often find us months or even years before they're ready to apply for benefits. Your job, together with our Growth Marketing and Product teams, is to make sure we're useful to them the entire time, so that when they're ready, Atticus is the obvious choice.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As we expand into new verticals, you’ll partner with our vertical GMs and Growth Product team to evolve our core site experience into one that delivers for each of our vertical audiences.</p><h2><br />You’ll be successful in this role if…</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You’ve spent 6-9 years in digital marketing, with at least 3 in a lead role owning a website P&amp;L or equivalent</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You’ve delivered demonstrable wins in SEO and content-led growth, ideally at a DTC brand with a long consideration cycle (health, wellness, fintech, education, legal services). If you can point to organic traffic charts that go up and to the right and tell us exactly why, we want to talk.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You have strong conversion chops. You've A/B tested landing pages, rebuilt funnels, and have strong opinions about what makes a vertical landing page convert. You can defend those opinions with data.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You have fluency in GEO/AEO. Search is changing fast. You're already thinking about AI Overviews, LLM citations, and what discovery looks like in 2027.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You are a strong writer. Not because you'll write every article, but because the brief is the artifact that determines whether content wins. Yours need to be excellent.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfort partnering with lifecycle. This role is not a silo. The best work here happens at the seam between digital and lifecycle, and you should be excited about that.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">AI-native instincts. You should feel like this job is twice as possible with the AI tooling available today than it was two years ago.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>Why Atticus</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>The work matters.</strong> Every conversion is a person who needs help finding legal representation to move forward.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You'll have real ownership</strong>. This is the senior digital seat reporting to the CMO, and the website is yours to shape.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You'll be surrounded by serious operators.</strong> Stanford- and Harvard-trained lawyers, an experienced exec team, and a marketing organization that takes craft seriously.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>We're well-funded and growing fast.</strong> $100M+ raised, hundreds of thousands of clients served, and a clear path to category leadership.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Remote-first with real connection</strong>. HQ in LA, team distributed across the US, with regular travel for in-person work.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are strongly committed to building a diverse team. If you’re from a background that’s underrepresented in tech, we’d love to meet you.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2>Salary and Benefits</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare opportunity to join a startup that has strong traction (substantial funding, well-respected backers, tremendous growth, and many happy customers) but is still small enough that you can have a huge impact and play a role in shaping our culture.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We’re a certified B Corporation tackling a critical social problem. Our mission to help people in need drives everything we do, and your work here will touch many lives.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We offer competitive pay — including equity — and generous benefits:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Medical and dental insurance with 100% of employee premiums covered</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">15 vacation days &amp; ~20 paid holidays each year (including two weeks at end-of-year)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Free membership to OneMedical</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$600/year reimbursable stipend for internet service</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$1,000 reimbursable stipend for education and training outside of work</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Up to $1,200/year student loan repayment assistance</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">401(k) and optional HSA/FSA</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Humble, thoughtful, smart, fun colleagues</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We anticipate the base salary band for this role will be between $145,000 to $180,000 in addition to equity and benefits. The salary at offer will be determined by a number of factors such as candidate’s experience, knowledge, skills and abilities, as well as internal equity among our team.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>Location</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This job is fully remote and we’re committed to empowering everyone with flexibility. Work remotely, and travel to LA (on the company dime) as needed to be with your colleagues – usually quarterly, plus offsites. We care a lot about building a great culture and we think some interactions need to happen in person, so we put a lot of thought into retreats, offsites, and other ways to gather.</p>","descriptionPlain":"ABOUT ATTICUS\n\nAt any given time, 16 million Americans are experiencing a serious injury or illness that requires urgent help from the legal system or the government. For many, it’s not just a health crisis – it’s the start of a bureaucratic nightmare. The right help could change their lives, but many never get it.\n\nAtticus exists to change that.\n\nWe're a new kind of law firm that helps sick, injured, and wronged Americans access the benefits designed to protect them — from Social Security disability insurance to workers' comp to insurance settlements. In six years, we've helped hundreds of thousands of people access more than $10 billion in life-changing aid, but our work is far from complete.\n\nWe've raised over $100 million from Fika, Forerunner, GV, and True Ventures. We closed our Series C in April 2025, so we're well-funded and investing in growth.\n\n\n\nABOUT THE ROLE\n\nAs the Head of Web and Organic Growth, you'll own our digital front door, including the homepage, vertical landing pages, our blog, and lead-magnets. You'll set the strategy to bring prospective clients to Atticus.com http://Atticus.com from organic and AI search. You’ll decide what they read, what they trust, and how they move from learning about Atticus to talking with one of our client advocates. You'll write the briefs that shape our blog content and the requirements that drive our SEO and GEO prominence. You'll work closely with our editorial team to commission content that ranks and genuinely helps people in need.\n\nThis is a high-leverage seat. Our prospective clients often find us months or even years before they're ready to apply for benefits. Your job, together with our Growth Marketing and Product teams, is to make sure we're useful to them the entire time, so that when they're ready, Atticus is the obvious choice.\n\nAs we expand into new verticals, you’ll partner with our vertical GMs and Growth Product team to evolve our core site experience into one that delivers for each of our vertical audiences.\n\n\n\nYOU’LL BE SUCCESSFUL IN THIS ROLE IF…\n\n\n\n - You’ve spent 6-9 years in digital marketing, with at least 3 in a lead role owning a website P&L or equivalent\n\n - You’ve delivered demonstrable wins in SEO and content-led growth, ideally at a DTC brand with a long consideration cycle (health, wellness, fintech, education, legal services). If you can point to organic traffic charts that go up and to the right and tell us exactly why, we want to talk.\n\n - You have strong conversion chops. You've A/B tested landing pages, rebuilt funnels, and have strong opinions about what makes a vertical landing page convert. You can defend those opinions with data.\n\n - You have fluency in GEO/AEO. Search is changing fast. You're already thinking about AI Overviews, LLM citations, and what discovery looks like in 2027.\n\n - You are a strong writer. Not because you'll write every article, but because the brief is the artifact that determines whether content wins. Yours need to be excellent.\n\n - Comfort partnering with lifecycle. This role is not a silo. The best work here happens at the seam between digital and lifecycle, and you should be excited about that.\n\n - AI-native instincts. You should feel like this job is twice as possible with the AI tooling available today than it was two years ago.\n\n\n\n\nWHY ATTICUS\n\n - The work matters. Every conversion is a person who needs help finding legal representation to move forward.\n\n - You'll have real ownership. This is the senior digital seat reporting to the CMO, and the website is yours to shape.\n\n - You'll be surrounded by serious operators. Stanford- and Harvard-trained lawyers, an experienced exec team, and a marketing organization that takes craft seriously.\n\n - We're well-funded and growing fast. $100M+ raised, hundreds of thousands of clients served, and a clear path to category leadership.\n\n - Remote-first with real connection. HQ in LA, team distributed across the US, with regular travel for in-person work.\n\nWe are strongly committed to building a diverse team. If you’re from a background that’s underrepresented in tech, we’d love to meet you.\n\n \n\n\nSALARY AND BENEFITS\n\nThis is a rare opportunity to join a startup that has strong traction (substantial funding, well-respected backers, tremendous growth, and many happy customers) but is still small enough that you can have a huge impact and play a role in shaping our culture.\n\nWe’re a certified B Corporation tackling a critical social problem. Our mission to help people in need drives everything we do, and your work here will touch many lives.\n\nWe offer competitive pay — including equity — and generous benefits:\n\n - Medical and dental insurance with 100% of employee premiums covered\n\n - 15 vacation days & ~20 paid holidays each year (including two weeks at end-of-year)\n\n - Free membership to OneMedical\n\n - $600/year reimbursable stipend for internet service\n\n - $1,000 reimbursable stipend for education and training outside of work\n\n - Up to $1,200/year student loan repayment assistance\n\n - 401(k) and optional HSA/FSA\n\n - Humble, thoughtful, smart, fun colleagues\n\nWe anticipate the base salary band for this role will be between $145,000 to $180,000 in addition to equity and benefits. The salary at offer will be determined by a number of factors such as candidate’s experience, knowledge, skills and abilities, as well as internal equity among our team.\n\n\n\n\nLOCATION\n\nThis job is fully remote and we’re committed to empowering everyone with flexibility. Work remotely, and travel to LA (on the company dime) as needed to be with your colleagues – usually quarterly, plus offsites. We care a lot about building a great culture and we think some interactions need to happen in person, so we put a lot of thought into retreats, offsites, and other ways to gather.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"edd6c007-7209-4aea-b784-9f2fd96af64d","title":"Engineering Manager, Growth","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-27T19:36:49.635+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Los Angeles"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/atticus/edd6c007-7209-4aea-b784-9f2fd96af64d","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/atticus/edd6c007-7209-4aea-b784-9f2fd96af64d/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About Atticus</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At any given time, 16 million Americans are experiencing a crisis that requires urgent help from our legal system or government. The right assistance could transform their lives. But today, most never get it.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our mission is to tear down barriers between people in crisis and the aid they deserve. In the last six years, we’ve become the leading platform connecting people with disabilities to government benefits. We also help victims of accidents, misconduct, and violence get compensation from insurance. So far, we’ve helped hundreds of thousands of people access over $10 billion in life-changing aid —and earned over 20,000 five-star reviews. And we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We've raised more than $100 million from top VC firms like Fika, Forerunner, Google Ventures, and True Ventures, and we’re on our way to creating a category defining business assisting needy Americans.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>The Job</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As the Engineering Manager for our Growth Pod, you will lead a full-stack product pod, reporting directly to Toby, our VP of Engineering. You will be accountable for both the health and growth of the team, and what it delivers. That means shaping an ambitious roadmap and directly driving the work to get there.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The Growth Pod is staffed with four full-stack engineers, a PM, a designer, and a data scientist who all share the same mission and goals: delivering experiences to help our clients find Atticus and understand how we can help them in a moment of crisis. The team operates on a rapid experimentation cadence, constantly testing new ideas and making data-driven decisions about what works best.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Engineering Managers at Atticus are hands-on leaders. In addition to owning your team’s roadmap, you’ll shape your team’s culture and processes, have an active hand in developing the careers of the people you manage, and be actively involved in the day to day technical work your team ships. EMs here aren’t typically our most senior technical contributors, but you should expect to be directly accountable for the quality of your team’s output and closely involved in coaching their technical work. That means staying close to the code; we want you reviewing PRs, weighing in on architecture, and diving into the details alongside your teammates when that's the right call.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Qualifications</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Required</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You've managed a team of at least three engineers for more than a year.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You've grown engineers, including senior ICs and people early in their careers. You're also able to have hard performance conversations when someone isn't meeting expectations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You've worked in a high-performing product organization, with strong PMs and designers, and you know what it means for engineers to own product outcomes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You've operated with ambiguity and limited resources, either at a startup like ours or by carving that out inside a larger company.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You've been using AI coding tools seriously in your own work over the past year, and have a view on where they help and how to get the most out of them without shipping slop.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You’re hands-on. You write code, review it, and have opinions about how systems get built.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Nice To Have</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Expertise in A/B testing, experiment design, and growth-style rapid iterative product development.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hands-on proficiency with our core stack: Go, TypeScript and Next.js, Temporal, or GCP. (Though, we care more that you can ramp quickly on technical context than that you've used these specific tools).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Background in an industry with complex professional workflows, such as legal, healthcare, or financial services.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are strongly committed to building a diverse team. If you’re from a background that’s underrepresented in tech, we’d love to meet you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Salary and Benefits</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare opportunity to join a startup that has strong traction (substantial funding, well-respected backers, tremendous growth, and many happy customers) but is still small enough that you can have a huge impact and play a role in shaping our culture.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We’re a certified B Corporation tackling a critical social problem. Our mission to help people in need drives everything we do, and your work here will touch many lives.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We offer competitive pay — including equity for all employees — and generous benefits:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Medical and dental insurance with 100% of premiums covered for employees and their families</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">15 vacation days &amp; ~20 paid holidays each year (including two weeks at end-of-year)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Free membership to OneMedical</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$600/year internet stipend</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$1,000/year reimbursable stipend for education and training outside of work</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Up to $1,200/year student loan repayment assistance</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">401(k) and optional HSA/FSA</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Humble, thoughtful, smart, fun colleagues</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We anticipate the base salary band for this role will be between $195,500 and $264,500 in addition to equity and benefits. The salary at offer will be determined by a number of factors such as candidate’s experience, knowledge, skills and abilities, as well as internal equity among our team.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This job is fully remote and we’re committed to empowering everyone with flexibility. Work remotely, and travel to LA (on the company dime) as needed to be with your colleagues – usually quarterly, plus offsites. We care a lot about building a great culture and we think some interactions need to happen in person, so we put a lot of thought into retreats, offsites, and other ways to gather.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p>","descriptionPlain":"About Atticus\n\nAt any given time, 16 million Americans are experiencing a crisis that requires urgent help from our legal system or government. The right assistance could transform their lives. But today, most never get it.\n\nOur mission is to tear down barriers between people in crisis and the aid they deserve. In the last six years, we’ve become the leading platform connecting people with disabilities to government benefits. We also help victims of accidents, misconduct, and violence get compensation from insurance. So far, we’ve helped hundreds of thousands of people access over $10 billion in life-changing aid —and earned over 20,000 five-star reviews. And we’re just getting started.\n\nWe've raised more than $100 million from top VC firms like Fika, Forerunner, Google Ventures, and True Ventures, and we’re on our way to creating a category defining business assisting needy Americans.\n\nThe Job\n\nAs the Engineering Manager for our Growth Pod, you will lead a full-stack product pod, reporting directly to Toby, our VP of Engineering. You will be accountable for both the health and growth of the team, and what it delivers. That means shaping an ambitious roadmap and directly driving the work to get there.\n\nThe Growth Pod is staffed with four full-stack engineers, a PM, a designer, and a data scientist who all share the same mission and goals: delivering experiences to help our clients find Atticus and understand how we can help them in a moment of crisis. The team operates on a rapid experimentation cadence, constantly testing new ideas and making data-driven decisions about what works best.\n\nEngineering Managers at Atticus are hands-on leaders. In addition to owning your team’s roadmap, you’ll shape your team’s culture and processes, have an active hand in developing the careers of the people you manage, and be actively involved in the day to day technical work your team ships. EMs here aren’t typically our most senior technical contributors, but you should expect to be directly accountable for the quality of your team’s output and closely involved in coaching their technical work. That means staying close to the code; we want you reviewing PRs, weighing in on architecture, and diving into the details alongside your teammates when that's the right call.\n\nQualifications\n\nRequired\n\n - You've managed a team of at least three engineers for more than a year.\n\n - You've grown engineers, including senior ICs and people early in their careers. You're also able to have hard performance conversations when someone isn't meeting expectations.\n\n - You've worked in a high-performing product organization, with strong PMs and designers, and you know what it means for engineers to own product outcomes.\n\n - You've operated with ambiguity and limited resources, either at a startup like ours or by carving that out inside a larger company.\n\n - You've been using AI coding tools seriously in your own work over the past year, and have a view on where they help and how to get the most out of them without shipping slop.\n\n - You’re hands-on. You write code, review it, and have opinions about how systems get built.\n\nNice To Have\n\n - Expertise in A/B testing, experiment design, and growth-style rapid iterative product development.\n\n - Hands-on proficiency with our core stack: Go, TypeScript and Next.js, Temporal, or GCP. (Though, we care more that you can ramp quickly on technical context than that you've used these specific tools).\n\n - Background in an industry with complex professional workflows, such as legal, healthcare, or financial services.\n\nWe are strongly committed to building a diverse team. If you’re from a background that’s underrepresented in tech, we’d love to meet you.\n\nSalary and Benefits\n\nThis is a rare opportunity to join a startup that has strong traction (substantial funding, well-respected backers, tremendous growth, and many happy customers) but is still small enough that you can have a huge impact and play a role in shaping our culture.\n\nWe’re a certified B Corporation tackling a critical social problem. Our mission to help people in need drives everything we do, and your work here will touch many lives.\n\nWe offer competitive pay — including equity for all employees — and generous benefits:\n\n - Medical and dental insurance with 100% of premiums covered for employees and their families\n\n - 15 vacation days & ~20 paid holidays each year (including two weeks at end-of-year)\n\n - Free membership to OneMedical\n\n - $600/year internet stipend\n\n - $1,000/year reimbursable stipend for education and training outside of work\n\n - Up to $1,200/year student loan repayment assistance\n\n - 401(k) and optional HSA/FSA\n\n - Humble, thoughtful, smart, fun colleagues\n\nWe anticipate the base salary band for this role will be between $195,500 and $264,500 in addition to equity and benefits. The salary at offer will be determined by a number of factors such as candidate’s experience, knowledge, skills and abilities, as well as internal equity among our team.\n\nLocation\n\nThis job is fully remote and we’re committed to empowering everyone with flexibility. Work remotely, and travel to LA (on the company dime) as needed to be with your colleagues – usually quarterly, plus offsites. We care a lot about building a great culture and we think some interactions need to happen in person, so we put a lot of thought into retreats, offsites, and other ways to gather.\n\n","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"03ed28c5-f496-4638-865d-302e895ccaaf","title":"Senior Engineering Manager","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-27T16:23:51.054+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Los Angeles"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/atticus/03ed28c5-f496-4638-865d-302e895ccaaf","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/atticus/03ed28c5-f496-4638-865d-302e895ccaaf/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At any given time, 16 million Americans are experiencing a crisis that requires urgent help from our legal system or government. The right assistance could transform their lives. But today, most never get it.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Our mission is to tear down barriers between people in crisis and the aid they deserve. In the last six years, we’ve become the leading platform connecting people with disabilities to government benefits. We also help victims of accidents, misconduct, and violence get compensation from insurance. So far, we’ve helped hundreds of thousands of people access over $10 billion in life-changing aid —and earned over 20,000 five-star reviews. And we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We've raised more than $100 million from top VC firms like Fika, Forerunner, Google Ventures, and True Ventures, and we’re on our way to creating a category defining business assisting needy Americans.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>The Job</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Senior Engineering Manager at Atticus, you will own one of our product pods, reporting directly to Toby, our VP of Engineering. You will be accountable for both the health and growth of your team, and what it delivers. That means shaping an ambitious roadmap and directly driving the work to get there.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Each pod owns a piece of our business outright and is accountable for whether that piece works well for our clients. Your pod will be staffed as small cross-functional units with 4-6 engineers, a PM, and a designer, all focused around a shared mission and set of goals.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Engineering Managers at Atticus are hands-on leaders. In addition to owning your team’s roadmap, you'll shape your team’s culture and processes, have an active hand in developing the careers of the people you manage, and be actively involved in the day to day technical work your team ships. EMs here aren’t typically our most senior technical contributors, but you should expect to be directly accountable for the quality of your team’s output and closely involved in coaching their technical work. That means staying close to the code; we want you reviewing PRs, weighing in on architecture, and diving into the details alongside your teammates when that's the right call.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We’re actively hiring for multiple EM roles to support our growing team. Depending on your background and interests, you might work on:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Consumer product experimentation.</strong> Building intuitive and informative experiences to help people understand how Atticus can help them and keep them informed throughout the process.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Getting clients to the right lawyer.</strong> Honing the intake experience for people in crisis and optimizing the ML matching systems underneath it.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Scaling our tools for attorneys.</strong> Delivering software for the firms in our network and for our own in-house law firm, so cases get handled consistently and well.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>AI-native legal product.</strong> Early-stage product development to turn inefficient work lawyers and their staff do by hand today into scalable products and workflows.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Qualifications</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Required</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You've managed a team of at least three engineers for more than 3 years.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You've grown engineers, including senior ICs and people early in their careers. You've also able to have hard performance conversations when someone isn't meeting expectations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You've worked in a high-performing product organization, with strong PMs and designers, and you know what it means for engineers to own product outcomes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You've operated with ambiguity and limited resources, either at a startup like ours or by carving that out inside a larger company.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You've been using AI coding tools seriously in your own work over the past year, and have a view on where they help and how to get the most out of them without shipping slop.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You’re hands-on. You write code, review it, and have opinions about how systems get built.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Nice To Have</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience hiring and leading engineers through periods of rapid headcount growth.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hands-on proficiency with our core stack: Go, TypeScript and Next.js, Temporal, or GCP. (Though, we care more that you can ramp quickly on technical context than that you've used these specific tools).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Background in an industry with complex professional workflows, such as legal, healthcare, or financial services.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are strongly committed to building a diverse team. If you’re from a background that’s underrepresented in tech, we’d love to meet you.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Salary and Benefits</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare opportunity to join a startup that has strong traction (substantial funding, well-respected backers, tremendous growth, and many happy customers) but is still small enough that you can have a huge impact and play a role in shaping our culture.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We’re a certified B Corporation tackling a critical social problem. Our mission to help people in need drives everything we do, and your work here will touch many lives.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We offer competitive pay — including equity for all employees — and generous benefits:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Medical and dental insurance with 100% of premiums covered for employees and their families</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">15 vacation days &amp; ~20 paid holidays each year (including two weeks at end-of-year)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Free membership to OneMedical</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$600/year internet stipend</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$1,000/year reimbursable stipend for education and training outside of work</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Up to $1,200/year student loan repayment assistance</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">401(k) and optional HSA/FSA</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Humble, thoughtful, smart, fun colleagues</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We anticipate the base salary band for this role will be between $195,000 and $264,500 in addition to equity and benefits. The salary at offer will be determined by a number of factors such as candidate’s experience, knowledge, skills and abilities, as well as internal equity among our team.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Location</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This job is fully remote and we’re committed to empowering everyone with flexibility. Work remotely, and travel to LA (on the company dime) as needed to be with your colleagues – usually quarterly, plus offsites. We care a lot about building a great culture and we think some interactions need to happen in person, so we put a lot of thought into retreats, offsites, and other ways to gather.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p>","descriptionPlain":"At any given time, 16 million Americans are experiencing a crisis that requires urgent help from our legal system or government. The right assistance could transform their lives. But today, most never get it.\n\nOur mission is to tear down barriers between people in crisis and the aid they deserve. In the last six years, we’ve become the leading platform connecting people with disabilities to government benefits. We also help victims of accidents, misconduct, and violence get compensation from insurance. So far, we’ve helped hundreds of thousands of people access over $10 billion in life-changing aid —and earned over 20,000 five-star reviews. And we’re just getting started.\n\nWe've raised more than $100 million from top VC firms like Fika, Forerunner, Google Ventures, and True Ventures, and we’re on our way to creating a category defining business assisting needy Americans.\n\nThe Job\n\nAs a Senior Engineering Manager at Atticus, you will own one of our product pods, reporting directly to Toby, our VP of Engineering. You will be accountable for both the health and growth of your team, and what it delivers. That means shaping an ambitious roadmap and directly driving the work to get there.\n\nEach pod owns a piece of our business outright and is accountable for whether that piece works well for our clients. Your pod will be staffed as small cross-functional units with 4-6 engineers, a PM, and a designer, all focused around a shared mission and set of goals.\n\nEngineering Managers at Atticus are hands-on leaders. In addition to owning your team’s roadmap, you'll shape your team’s culture and processes, have an active hand in developing the careers of the people you manage, and be actively involved in the day to day technical work your team ships. EMs here aren’t typically our most senior technical contributors, but you should expect to be directly accountable for the quality of your team’s output and closely involved in coaching their technical work. That means staying close to the code; we want you reviewing PRs, weighing in on architecture, and diving into the details alongside your teammates when that's the right call.\n\nWe’re actively hiring for multiple EM roles to support our growing team. Depending on your background and interests, you might work on:\n\n - Consumer product experimentation. Building intuitive and informative experiences to help people understand how Atticus can help them and keep them informed throughout the process.\n\n - Getting clients to the right lawyer. Honing the intake experience for people in crisis and optimizing the ML matching systems underneath it.\n\n - Scaling our tools for attorneys. Delivering software for the firms in our network and for our own in-house law firm, so cases get handled consistently and well.\n\n - AI-native legal product. Early-stage product development to turn inefficient work lawyers and their staff do by hand today into scalable products and workflows.\n\nQualifications\n\nRequired\n\n - You've managed a team of at least three engineers for more than 3 years.\n\n - You've grown engineers, including senior ICs and people early in their careers. You've also able to have hard performance conversations when someone isn't meeting expectations.\n\n - You've worked in a high-performing product organization, with strong PMs and designers, and you know what it means for engineers to own product outcomes.\n\n - You've operated with ambiguity and limited resources, either at a startup like ours or by carving that out inside a larger company.\n\n - You've been using AI coding tools seriously in your own work over the past year, and have a view on where they help and how to get the most out of them without shipping slop.\n\n - You’re hands-on. You write code, review it, and have opinions about how systems get built.\n\nNice To Have\n\n - Experience hiring and leading engineers through periods of rapid headcount growth.\n\n - Hands-on proficiency with our core stack: Go, TypeScript and Next.js, Temporal, or GCP. (Though, we care more that you can ramp quickly on technical context than that you've used these specific tools).\n\n - Background in an industry with complex professional workflows, such as legal, healthcare, or financial services.\n\nWe are strongly committed to building a diverse team. If you’re from a background that’s underrepresented in tech, we’d love to meet you.\n\nSalary and Benefits\n\nThis is a rare opportunity to join a startup that has strong traction (substantial funding, well-respected backers, tremendous growth, and many happy customers) but is still small enough that you can have a huge impact and play a role in shaping our culture.\n\nWe’re a certified B Corporation tackling a critical social problem. Our mission to help people in need drives everything we do, and your work here will touch many lives.\n\nWe offer competitive pay — including equity for all employees — and generous benefits:\n\n - Medical and dental insurance with 100% of premiums covered for employees and their families\n\n - 15 vacation days & ~20 paid holidays each year (including two weeks at end-of-year)\n\n - Free membership to OneMedical\n\n - $600/year internet stipend\n\n - $1,000/year reimbursable stipend for education and training outside of work\n\n - Up to $1,200/year student loan repayment assistance\n\n - 401(k) and optional HSA/FSA\n\n - Humble, thoughtful, smart, fun colleagues\n\nWe anticipate the base salary band for this role will be between $195,000 and $264,500 in addition to equity and benefits. The salary at offer will be determined by a number of factors such as candidate’s experience, knowledge, skills and abilities, as well as internal equity among our team.\n\nLocation\n\nThis job is fully remote and we’re committed to empowering everyone with flexibility. Work remotely, and travel to LA (on the company dime) as needed to be with your colleagues – usually quarterly, plus offsites. We care a lot about building a great culture and we think some interactions need to happen in person, so we put a lot of thought into retreats, offsites, and other ways to gather.\n\n","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"8553957b-aa32-460e-ac59-e605a6e1d4e2","title":"Paralegal","department":"Direct Representation","team":"Direct Representation","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"Remote","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-31T19:56:24.759+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"California","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"Los Angeles"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/atticus/8553957b-aa32-460e-ac59-e605a6e1d4e2","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/atticus/8553957b-aa32-460e-ac59-e605a6e1d4e2/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2><strong>About Atticus</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At any given time, 16 million Americans are experiencing a crisis that requires urgent help from our legal system or government. The right assistance could transform their lives. But today, most never get it.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Atticus makes it easy for any sick or injured American to get life-changing aid. Our mission is to tear down barriers between people in crisis and the aid they deserve. In the last six years, we’ve become the leading platform connecting people with disabilities to government benefits.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We also help victims of accidents, misconduct, and violence get compensation from insurance.<br />So far, we’ve helped hundreds of thousands of people access over $10 billion in life-changing aid —and earned over 20,000 five-star reviews. And we’re just getting started.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We've raised more than $100 million from top VC firms like Fika, Forerunner, Google Ventures, and True Ventures, and we’re on our way to creating a category defining business assisting needy Americans.</p><h2><strong>The Job</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Each day, thousands of people seek our help getting disability benefits or insurance compensation. They’re intimidated by the process, unsure where to turn, and desperate for good advice.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">As a Paralegal at Atticus, your job is to get them on the right path. This job is different from that of a traditional paralegal. The job mixes responsibilities in any good paralegal’s comfort zone (build client relationships; keep your caseload moving; and collaborate with attorneys on case strategy) with those unique to being an operator in a fast-growing tech company (help Marketing source clients who’d be great in testimonials, or user test new tools for Product).</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">In a typical week you might do any of the following:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Interview a client, analyze their medical records, and draft a persuasive memo arguing why the SSA should consider them disabled.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work with a client’s local representative to run down missing paperwork at SSA</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Take on an inefficient workflow that’s slowing the team down (e.g., processing case updates), scope an improvement, get team buy-in, and execute the improvement.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This role is a rare opportunity to join a fast-growing Series C startup and do meaningful social impact work. It’s designed to be a path to (a) staying at Atticus and advancing on the Representation Lab team, or (b) heading to law school or business school (we'll help you with applications and we write great recs).</p><h2><strong>Qualifications</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Required:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You have experience in a professional role that required a substantial amount of client-facing work (like a case manager) or lawyer-facing work (like a paralegal).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You are a resourceful team-player ready to dive into a scrappy startup environment where you will learn quickly and get your hands dirty.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You are comfortable in a variety of interpersonal conversations; you can be empathetic and kind when speaking with people in a moment of crisis, and can be thoughtful and organized when interacting with attorneys.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You have a demonstrated commitment to doing good and helping people.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Bonus / Nice-to-Have:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You have professional experience helping others apply for government benefits.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You have experience at a startup or other fast-paced, agile environment.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are strongly committed to building a diverse team. If you’re from a background that’s underrepresented in tech, we’d love to meet you.</p><h2><strong>Salary and Benefits</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a rare opportunity to join a startup that has strong traction (substantial funding, well-respected backers, tremendous growth, and many happy customers) but is still small enough that you can have a huge impact and play a role in shaping our culture.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We’re a certified B Corporation tackling a critical social problem. Our mission to help people in need drives everything we do, and your work here will touch many lives.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We offer competitive pay — including equity for every employee — and generous benefits:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Medical and dental insurance with 100% of employees and their families premiums covered</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">15 vacation days &amp; ~20 paid holidays each year (including two weeks at the end-of-year)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Free membership to OneMedical</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$600/year internet stipend</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$1,000/year reimbursable stipend for education and training outside of work</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Up to $1,200/year student loan repayment assistance</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">401(k) and optional HSA/FSA</p></li></ul><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Humble, thoughtful, smart, fun colleagues</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We anticipate the base salary band for this role will be between $75,000 and $90,000 in addition to equity and benefits. The salary at offer will be determined by a number of factors such as candidate’s experience, knowledge, skills and abilities, as well as internal equity among our team.</p><h2><strong>Location</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This job is fully remote and we’re committed to empowering everyone with flexibility. Work remotely, and travel to LA (on the company dime) as needed to be with your colleagues – usually quarterly, plus offsites. We care a lot about building a great culture and we think some interactions need to happen in person, so we put a lot of thought into retreats, offsites, and other ways to gather.</p>","descriptionPlain":"ABOUT ATTICUS\n\nAt any given time, 16 million Americans are experiencing a crisis that requires urgent help from our legal system or government. The right assistance could transform their lives. But today, most never get it.\n\nAtticus makes it easy for any sick or injured American to get life-changing aid. Our mission is to tear down barriers between people in crisis and the aid they deserve. In the last six years, we’ve become the leading platform connecting people with disabilities to government benefits.\n\nWe also help victims of accidents, misconduct, and violence get compensation from insurance.\nSo far, we’ve helped hundreds of thousands of people access over $10 billion in life-changing aid —and earned over 20,000 five-star reviews. And we’re just getting started.\n\nWe've raised more than $100 million from top VC firms like Fika, Forerunner, Google Ventures, and True Ventures, and we’re on our way to creating a category defining business assisting needy Americans.\n\n\nTHE JOB\n\nEach day, thousands of people seek our help getting disability benefits or insurance compensation. They’re intimidated by the process, unsure where to turn, and desperate for good advice.\n\nAs a Paralegal at Atticus, your job is to get them on the right path. This job is different from that of a traditional paralegal. The job mixes responsibilities in any good paralegal’s comfort zone (build client relationships; keep your caseload moving; and collaborate with attorneys on case strategy) with those unique to being an operator in a fast-growing tech company (help Marketing source clients who’d be great in testimonials, or user test new tools for Product).\n\nIn a typical week you might do any of the following:\n\n - Interview a client, analyze their medical records, and draft a persuasive memo arguing why the SSA should consider them disabled.\n\n - Work with a client’s local representative to run down missing paperwork at SSA\n\n - Take on an inefficient workflow that’s slowing the team down (e.g., processing case updates), scope an improvement, get team buy-in, and execute the improvement.\n\nThis role is a rare opportunity to join a fast-growing Series C startup and do meaningful social impact work. It’s designed to be a path to (a) staying at Atticus and advancing on the Representation Lab team, or (b) heading to law school or business school (we'll help you with applications and we write great recs).\n\n\nQUALIFICATIONS\n\nRequired:\n\n - You have experience in a professional role that required a substantial amount of client-facing work (like a case manager) or lawyer-facing work (like a paralegal).\n\n - You are a resourceful team-player ready to dive into a scrappy startup environment where you will learn quickly and get your hands dirty.\n\n - You are comfortable in a variety of interpersonal conversations; you can be empathetic and kind when speaking with people in a moment of crisis, and can be thoughtful and organized when interacting with attorneys.\n\n - You have a demonstrated commitment to doing good and helping people.\n\nBonus / Nice-to-Have:\n\n - You have professional experience helping others apply for government benefits.\n\n - You have experience at a startup or other fast-paced, agile environment.\n\nWe are strongly committed to building a diverse team. If you’re from a background that’s underrepresented in tech, we’d love to meet you.\n\n\nSALARY AND BENEFITS\n\nThis is a rare opportunity to join a startup that has strong traction (substantial funding, well-respected backers, tremendous growth, and many happy customers) but is still small enough that you can have a huge impact and play a role in shaping our culture.\n\nWe’re a certified B Corporation tackling a critical social problem. Our mission to help people in need drives everything we do, and your work here will touch many lives.\n\nWe offer competitive pay — including equity for every employee — and generous benefits:\n\n - Medical and dental insurance with 100% of employees and their families premiums covered\n\n - 15 vacation days & ~20 paid holidays each year (including two weeks at the end-of-year)\n\n - Free membership to OneMedical\n\n - $600/year internet stipend\n\n - $1,000/year reimbursable stipend for education and training outside of work\n\n - Up to $1,200/year student loan repayment assistance\n\n - 401(k) and optional HSA/FSA\n\n - Humble, thoughtful, smart, fun colleagues\n\nWe anticipate the base salary band for this role will be between $75,000 and $90,000 in addition to equity and benefits. The salary at offer will be determined by a number of factors such as candidate’s experience, knowledge, skills and abilities, as well as internal equity among our team.\n\n\nLOCATION\n\nThis job is fully remote and we’re committed to empowering everyone with flexibility. Work remotely, and travel to LA (on the company dime) as needed to be with your colleagues – usually quarterly, plus offsites. We care a lot about building a great culture and we think some interactions need to happen in person, so we put a lot of thought into retreats, offsites, and other ways to gather.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}}],"apiVersion":"1"}